1
00:00:42,272 --> 00:00:46,067
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:46,151 --> 00:00:47,777
‎[door creaking]

3
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:02,876
‎[Ha-ri] ‎Gotcha, Cheon Yeo-ri.

4
00:01:03,918 --> 00:01:05,670
‎[breathes deeply]

5
00:01:10,717 --> 00:01:12,635
‎[clanging]

6
00:01:16,055 --> 00:01:17,891
‎[wind gusting]

7
00:01:39,954 --> 00:01:41,789
‎EPISODE 8

8
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:52,717
‎[gasps]

9
00:01:58,223 --> 00:01:59,974
‎[tense music playing]

10
00:02:00,058 --> 00:02:02,727
‎[faint ghostly shrieking]

11
00:02:13,905 --> 00:02:16,699
‎[sirens wailing]

12
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:40,682
‎Sorry I didn't answer you.

13
00:02:40,765 --> 00:02:42,850
‎I was heading into court,
‎so I couldn't pick up the phone.

14
00:02:43,476 --> 00:02:46,229
‎But when I saw your text, I immediately
‎sent the police to the flower shop.

15
00:02:46,312 --> 00:02:47,689
‎[sighs] Great.

16
00:02:48,273 --> 00:02:50,900
‎Uh, so, is there a body in there, Yeo-Ri?

17
00:02:53,528 --> 00:02:55,863
‎There, move in. Come on, let's go.

18
00:02:58,116 --> 00:02:59,242
‎-He's in here.
‎-Where?

19
00:02:59,325 --> 00:03:00,326
‎Here.

20
00:03:01,035 --> 00:03:02,662
‎[officer] We've got something in here!

21
00:03:03,746 --> 00:03:05,957
‎[dramatic music playing]

22
00:03:07,291 --> 00:03:08,292
‎[Ha-ri] Whoa.

23
00:03:20,513 --> 00:03:23,266
‎How the heck did she know
‎his body was in there?

24
00:03:24,434 --> 00:03:25,309
‎Oh, wait.

25
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:28,271
‎This is just like
‎when she found Jang Eun-ju.

26
00:03:32,734 --> 00:03:35,778
‎Let me go! Get off me! I told you,
‎I'm Si-o, what are you doing?

27
00:03:36,404 --> 00:03:37,822
‎Come on, let me go!

28
00:03:38,698 --> 00:03:39,824
‎Hey! Can you just--

29
00:03:40,408 --> 00:03:41,743
‎[Ko] You must've been really shocked.

30
00:03:49,208 --> 00:03:50,877
‎[siren warbles]

31
00:03:58,259 --> 00:03:59,635
‎Seriously, Cheon Yeo-ri…

32
00:04:00,219 --> 00:04:01,429
‎What the heck?

33
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:05,933
‎Is it finally time I drop this bomb
‎for everyone to see?

34
00:04:08,144 --> 00:04:10,813
‎My daughter Ha-ri filmed this herself.

35
00:04:11,522 --> 00:04:14,150
‎That seems pretty suspicious,
‎wouldn't you agree?

36
00:04:15,109 --> 00:04:16,110
‎[sighs]

37
00:04:16,194 --> 00:04:20,782
‎Don't get me wrong, maybe
‎an average person could behave like this.

38
00:04:20,865 --> 00:04:22,116
‎But not her.

39
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:25,119
‎Someone who could one day
‎run the Reina Group

40
00:04:25,203 --> 00:04:28,164
‎shouldn't be running around
‎doing absurd things like this.

41
00:04:28,247 --> 00:04:30,208
‎That is just unacceptable.
‎Don't you think?

42
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:32,543
‎With the group
‎at such a crucial crossroads,

43
00:04:32,627 --> 00:04:34,921
‎we can't afford
‎to face another public scandal.

44
00:04:35,505 --> 00:04:39,092
‎Six years ago was the engagement thing.
‎I remember how much the stock tanked.

45
00:04:39,175 --> 00:04:41,260
‎With that in mind, sir,

46
00:04:41,344 --> 00:04:44,889
‎we'd like to hold
‎a special shareholders' meeting soon.

47
00:04:44,972 --> 00:04:46,265
‎As soon as possible.

48
00:04:47,517 --> 00:04:49,977
‎We were hoping that you
‎and the other senior members

49
00:04:50,061 --> 00:04:52,897
‎who worked with the late chairman
‎would lend us your backing.

50
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:56,401
‎We'd be honored if you would
‎show us support, if you can.

51
00:04:56,484 --> 00:04:58,778
‎A special shareholders' meeting…

52
00:04:59,695 --> 00:05:00,530
‎Regarding what?

53
00:05:01,906 --> 00:05:05,993
‎Naturally, we're talking about
‎removing Reina's CEO.

54
00:05:06,077 --> 00:05:06,911
‎[knocking on door]

55
00:05:19,632 --> 00:05:21,968
‎-[sighs]
‎-So what did you want to talk about?

56
00:05:22,051 --> 00:05:24,720
‎You said you'd tell us once she got here.

57
00:05:24,804 --> 00:05:27,223
‎It's about what people
‎have been saying about Yeo-ri.

58
00:05:27,807 --> 00:05:30,143
‎Grandma, I thought
‎we should all watch this together.

59
00:05:42,029 --> 00:05:44,574
‎You know about
‎the whole Seung-jae incident.

60
00:05:44,657 --> 00:05:46,534
‎There were those photos of Yeo-ri
‎at the scene

61
00:05:46,617 --> 00:05:48,077
‎where Jang Eun-ju's body was found.

62
00:05:48,911 --> 00:05:52,582
‎It happened again this time.
‎Yeo-ri went there, and a body was found.

63
00:05:52,665 --> 00:05:55,251
‎She got the right abandoned building
‎and the exact room.

64
00:05:55,334 --> 00:05:57,253
‎It's crazy, like someone tipped her off.

65
00:05:58,671 --> 00:06:00,715
‎I heard the dead guy's name was Si-o.

66
00:06:00,798 --> 00:06:02,133
‎He was Reina's art director.

67
00:06:02,216 --> 00:06:03,384
‎Wasn't he?

68
00:06:06,095 --> 00:06:06,929
‎[sighs]

69
00:06:12,310 --> 00:06:13,811
‎It's true, I won't deny it.

70
00:06:15,062 --> 00:06:15,897
‎Si-o was killed.

71
00:06:17,398 --> 00:06:19,025
‎And that's exactly
‎where his body was found.

72
00:06:19,108 --> 00:06:21,444
‎Don't try to brush it off as
‎a coincidence this time. I won't buy it.

73
00:06:23,112 --> 00:06:25,198
‎Mr. Cha Gi-u was telling me
‎the exact same thing.

74
00:06:25,781 --> 00:06:28,326
‎She only got away with it
‎because he refused to talk.

75
00:06:28,409 --> 00:06:30,870
‎First the Jang Eun-ju case, and now this…

76
00:06:32,205 --> 00:06:36,250
‎How many times can this happen
‎before we stop calling it a coincidence?

77
00:06:41,005 --> 00:06:44,592
‎Grandma, it's no coincidence.
‎She's clearly still seeing ghosts.

78
00:06:44,675 --> 00:06:46,761
‎How can she lead the company
‎when she's running around

79
00:06:46,844 --> 00:06:49,305
‎chasing dead bodies
‎under the influence of those ghosts?

80
00:06:50,139 --> 00:06:51,307
‎What do you have to say?

81
00:06:52,683 --> 00:06:53,517
‎The truth is…

82
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:02,777
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk
‎sent me to that location.

83
00:07:03,694 --> 00:07:05,571
‎He knew Si-o was Reina's art director,

84
00:07:05,655 --> 00:07:09,200
‎and he needed someone to confirm
‎his identity, so he wanted me there.

85
00:07:09,867 --> 00:07:11,869
‎He was supposed to meet me at the site.

86
00:07:11,953 --> 00:07:13,829
‎But something came up. He got held up,

87
00:07:13,913 --> 00:07:15,456
‎and I got there before anyone else.

88
00:07:16,082 --> 00:07:18,960
‎Grandma, she's lying.
‎You know that, don't you?

89
00:07:19,043 --> 00:07:21,754
‎She made that up on the spot.
‎It doesn't even make sense.

90
00:07:21,837 --> 00:07:23,381
‎What doesn't make sense about it?

91
00:07:23,464 --> 00:07:24,840
‎And hold on a second.

92
00:07:25,508 --> 00:07:26,634
‎You were following me, weren't you?

93
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:30,846
‎I know exactly what you're trying
‎to achieve with these tricks.

94
00:07:30,930 --> 00:07:32,932
‎But unfortunately for you,

95
00:07:33,015 --> 00:07:34,267
‎they'll get you nowhere.

96
00:07:38,604 --> 00:07:39,730
‎Ha-ri.

97
00:07:39,814 --> 00:07:41,232
‎I'd like you to go.

98
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:44,694
‎[scoffs] Grandma, really?

99
00:08:00,751 --> 00:08:02,461
‎Yeo-ri, I'm disappointed.

100
00:08:03,087 --> 00:08:04,505
‎I don't care what happened.

101
00:08:04,589 --> 00:08:07,133
‎Don't give Ha-ri ammunition,
‎no matter what.

102
00:08:08,342 --> 00:08:09,552
‎I'm sorry, Grandma.

103
00:08:09,635 --> 00:08:12,013
‎I'm worried about Director Gong
‎and the old guard.

104
00:08:12,096 --> 00:08:15,016
‎They're going to bring this up again,
‎like they did six years ago.

105
00:08:18,019 --> 00:08:18,936
‎I'll tell you what…

106
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:22,189
‎uh, Prosecutor Ma.

107
00:08:22,773 --> 00:08:25,234
‎He has an impressive background.

108
00:08:25,318 --> 00:08:29,322
‎He's built up a solid reputation
‎in legal circles.

109
00:08:29,405 --> 00:08:30,573
‎He's also…

110
00:08:31,574 --> 00:08:33,075
‎Well, he's, um…

111
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,660
‎decent looking, I'd say.

112
00:08:35,536 --> 00:08:39,081
‎Let's pick a date
‎for the engagement ceremony.

113
00:08:39,165 --> 00:08:41,751
‎[melancholy music playing]

114
00:08:46,172 --> 00:08:48,507
‎[breathes deeply]

115
00:09:07,568 --> 00:09:08,653
‎Gang-uk, hi.

116
00:09:09,987 --> 00:09:11,155
‎I need to talk to you.

117
00:09:11,238 --> 00:09:12,365
‎Are you free tomorrow?

118
00:09:17,244 --> 00:09:18,371
‎[door opens]

119
00:09:21,374 --> 00:09:22,416
‎[Yeo-ri] You're here.

120
00:09:24,335 --> 00:09:26,420
‎[sighs] Siena Hall.

121
00:09:26,504 --> 00:09:28,506
‎I love this place. It's really nice.

122
00:09:28,589 --> 00:09:32,176
‎[Yeo-ri] My dad bought it for my mom as
‎a gift for their 10th wedding anniversary.

123
00:09:32,259 --> 00:09:34,637
‎[Gang-uk]
‎Oh. So it must mean a lot to you.

124
00:09:35,596 --> 00:09:36,972
‎How did the two of them meet?

125
00:09:38,307 --> 00:09:40,893
‎My dad studied architecture
‎in college, actually.

126
00:09:40,976 --> 00:09:42,395
‎Part of the course was in Europe,

127
00:09:42,478 --> 00:09:44,980
‎and during a holiday,
‎he visited Siena, Italy.

128
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:48,359
‎-He met my mom there.
‎-Hmm. Awesome.

129
00:09:48,442 --> 00:09:50,695
‎So it's called "Siena"
‎because that's where they met?

130
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:53,322
‎Wow, that's a really romantic story.

131
00:09:54,532 --> 00:09:57,910
‎[sighs] The sad thing is,
‎if Reina ends up going to my aunt,

132
00:09:58,619 --> 00:10:00,538
‎the first thing she'll do
‎is tear this place down.

133
00:10:01,622 --> 00:10:04,875
‎She's gonna build an art gallery
‎or something before long.

134
00:10:06,085 --> 00:10:07,670
‎I wouldn't be able to save it.

135
00:10:08,671 --> 00:10:10,589
‎Even though protecting this place
‎is all I want.

136
00:10:10,673 --> 00:10:12,425
‎No, we can't let that happen, Yeo-ri.

137
00:10:12,508 --> 00:10:14,343
‎I'll help you protect Siena.

138
00:10:15,928 --> 00:10:18,848
‎Ah. Those videos that Ha-ri took…

139
00:10:18,931 --> 00:10:20,182
‎Did they blow over?

140
00:10:21,475 --> 00:10:22,476
‎[sighs]

141
00:10:23,102 --> 00:10:25,354
‎Actually, no.
‎Funny you should mention that.

142
00:10:25,438 --> 00:10:27,064
‎It turned into a whole issue.

143
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:30,943
‎Now my grandma's pushing
‎for us to get engaged right away.

144
00:10:31,777 --> 00:10:33,696
‎Before the rumors get any worse.

145
00:10:35,156 --> 00:10:36,657
‎What should we do?

146
00:10:36,741 --> 00:10:38,492
‎-[sighs]
‎-Looks like we're, uh…

147
00:10:38,576 --> 00:10:41,579
‎We're gonna have to go through
‎with the engagement ceremony.

148
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:45,499
‎I know it's too much pressure
‎to put on you.

149
00:10:45,583 --> 00:10:47,168
‎You don't have to say yes.

150
00:10:52,423 --> 00:10:53,549
‎Not at all.

151
00:10:54,717 --> 00:10:56,010
‎I think it's a great idea.

152
00:10:56,093 --> 00:10:57,553
‎[romantic music playing]

153
00:10:57,636 --> 00:10:58,763
‎To be honest,

154
00:10:58,846 --> 00:11:01,474
‎I was kinda scared
‎to be around you at first.

155
00:11:02,683 --> 00:11:03,684
‎And the ghosts scared me, too.

156
00:11:05,644 --> 00:11:08,481
‎But then I noticed
‎the way you've been dealing with

157
00:11:08,564 --> 00:11:10,441
‎all this terrible stuff
‎completely on your own

158
00:11:10,524 --> 00:11:12,568
‎just to keep everyone around you safe.

159
00:11:13,235 --> 00:11:15,321
‎Not everyone could do something like that.

160
00:11:17,615 --> 00:11:18,782
‎You're incredible.

161
00:11:18,866 --> 00:11:21,243
‎And that's the kind of person you are.

162
00:11:21,327 --> 00:11:22,828
‎You're kind and warm-hearted.

163
00:11:25,539 --> 00:11:28,584
‎[sighs] I wish other people
‎could see that about you too.

164
00:11:28,667 --> 00:11:30,044
‎It's a shame they don't.

165
00:11:32,338 --> 00:11:33,297
‎And now,

166
00:11:34,632 --> 00:11:36,467
‎every single time I think about you,

167
00:11:37,343 --> 00:11:40,179
‎my heart feels
‎all warm and fuzzy, you know?

168
00:11:40,262 --> 00:11:42,181
‎And even the sky seems a little bluer.

169
00:11:44,558 --> 00:11:48,020
‎Just being able to stand here
‎looking at you feels like a gift.

170
00:11:49,522 --> 00:11:51,023
‎So of course I'm gonna say yes.

171
00:11:52,358 --> 00:11:53,442
‎I actually want to.

172
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,320
‎Because my feelings for you

173
00:11:57,154 --> 00:11:58,489
‎are genuine, Yeo-ri.

174
00:12:15,756 --> 00:12:19,134
‎Because my feelings for you
‎are genuine, Yeo-ri.

175
00:12:20,594 --> 00:12:23,097
‎[giggling]

176
00:12:24,682 --> 00:12:25,683
‎[knocking on door]

177
00:12:25,766 --> 00:12:26,850
‎[door opens]

178
00:12:27,977 --> 00:12:29,436
‎[Yeo-ri gasps]

179
00:12:32,439 --> 00:12:35,150
‎-You got a call from Singapore, Ms. Cheon.
‎-Really?

180
00:12:35,234 --> 00:12:37,236
‎They were hoping you'd let them know
‎by the end of the week

181
00:12:37,319 --> 00:12:38,946
‎whether you'll be coming or not.

182
00:12:39,029 --> 00:12:41,156
‎Oh, just tell them… [grunts]

183
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:43,158
‎…someone is definitely going.

184
00:12:43,242 --> 00:12:46,036
‎We'll let them know
‎whether I'll be the one who goes

185
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,871
‎or if we're sending Mr. Bong.

186
00:12:48,455 --> 00:12:50,416
‎-We'll keep them posted, all right?
‎-Yeah.

187
00:12:54,545 --> 00:12:56,130
‎-You can go now.
‎-Ah, okay.

188
00:13:00,509 --> 00:13:01,760
‎-[Hyeong-min] How are you?
‎-Hey.

189
00:13:03,554 --> 00:13:05,180
‎Huh? What happened?

190
00:13:05,264 --> 00:13:07,516
‎-Sprained your ankle?
‎-Yep, on the stairs.

191
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,269
‎Ah. Hyeong-min,
‎you got any pain relief patches?

192
00:13:10,352 --> 00:13:12,187
‎-I'm fine, I'm fine.
‎-I don't have anything.

193
00:13:12,271 --> 00:13:13,188
‎-Wait a minute.
‎-Huh?

194
00:13:13,272 --> 00:13:15,149
‎You know your way around
‎acupuncture, don't you?

195
00:13:15,232 --> 00:13:16,442
‎-[Gang-uk] Acupuncture?
‎-It's okay.

196
00:13:16,525 --> 00:13:18,277
‎Well, I do have a certification.
‎But how did you know?

197
00:13:18,902 --> 00:13:20,446
‎-I saw it in your car once.
‎-[scoffs]

198
00:13:21,155 --> 00:13:22,948
‎Yeah, I always carry it with me
‎just to be safe.

199
00:13:23,032 --> 00:13:24,158
‎Grandma's always worried--

200
00:13:24,241 --> 00:13:25,326
‎[gasps]

201
00:13:25,409 --> 00:13:26,410
‎Grandma!

202
00:13:27,328 --> 00:13:28,162
‎[groans]

203
00:13:28,245 --> 00:13:30,497
‎Why the sudden concern?
‎Is she sick or something?

204
00:13:30,581 --> 00:13:31,707
‎No, no, it's not that…

205
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:33,792
‎[groans] The Black Monkey.

206
00:13:35,252 --> 00:13:37,087
‎Pil-dong, what… what should I do now?

207
00:13:37,171 --> 00:13:39,214
‎What should you do about what?
‎Can you tell me what's going on?

208
00:13:39,298 --> 00:13:41,717
‎Well, listen, uh,
‎when you found your wife, how was it?

209
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,801
‎Um, was anyone against it?

210
00:13:42,885 --> 00:13:44,428
‎-Yeah, totally.
‎-Oh, yeah. For sure.

211
00:13:44,511 --> 00:13:46,263
‎-Because of the age difference.
‎-Ten years.

212
00:13:46,347 --> 00:13:47,473
‎-Hey, seven years.
‎-Oh, seven years. Yep.

213
00:13:47,556 --> 00:13:49,850
‎Seven… Seven years?
‎That means she's a year older than Yeo-ri.

214
00:13:50,643 --> 00:13:52,061
‎Pil-dong! What's her birth sign?

215
00:13:52,144 --> 00:13:53,812
‎-The Year of the Sheep.
‎-The Sheep?

216
00:13:53,896 --> 00:13:55,814
‎-Uh-huh.
‎-Year of the Sheep, that's one year older…

217
00:13:56,523 --> 00:13:57,733
‎-Pil-dong.
‎-Hmm?

218
00:13:57,816 --> 00:13:58,901
‎Please let me borrow your wife's ‎saju‎.

219
00:13:58,984 --> 00:14:00,819
‎You'd basically be saving my life,
‎all right?

220
00:14:01,487 --> 00:14:03,656
‎I'm sorry,
‎but I'm not gonna lend you anything

221
00:14:03,739 --> 00:14:06,075
‎-unless you tell me what's going on.
‎-Well, the thing is…

222
00:14:07,368 --> 00:14:09,286
‎I'm dying to get engaged.

223
00:14:10,287 --> 00:14:12,373
‎Oh, you're… Wait. What?

224
00:14:12,456 --> 00:14:14,958
‎-You're getting engaged, Gang-uk?
‎-Yeah.

225
00:14:15,042 --> 00:14:16,126
‎What on earth?

226
00:14:16,210 --> 00:14:17,169
‎-What are you talking about?
‎-Ow!

227
00:14:17,252 --> 00:14:18,253
‎-How did this even happen?
‎-Ow!

228
00:14:18,337 --> 00:14:21,715
‎-What's going on? Huh? Huh?
‎-Ow! Ow! Use your words! Ow.

229
00:14:21,799 --> 00:14:23,509
‎[winces, groans]

230
00:14:23,592 --> 00:14:26,178
‎If someone said you don't have
‎any manners, they wouldn't be wrong.

231
00:14:26,261 --> 00:14:28,639
‎Huh? [groans]

232
00:14:28,722 --> 00:14:31,600
‎You can't even get engaged without telling
‎your grandma, young man. How dare you?

233
00:14:31,684 --> 00:14:35,270
‎Huh? If you'd told me earlier,
‎I would've examined her properly.

234
00:14:35,354 --> 00:14:37,731
‎Were you trying to sneak
‎this engagement past me

235
00:14:37,815 --> 00:14:41,193
‎like a snake in the bushes, quiet and sly?

236
00:14:41,276 --> 00:14:43,487
‎-Huh?
‎-[sighs]

237
00:14:43,570 --> 00:14:46,615
‎Honestly, Grandma, I wouldn't
‎back out of this even if you said no.

238
00:14:46,699 --> 00:14:48,450
‎Okay? You would've scared her away.

239
00:14:48,534 --> 00:14:51,662
‎You would've put her on the spot
‎and scared her away, I'm sure of it.

240
00:14:52,246 --> 00:14:53,747
‎That's why I told her to do that.

241
00:14:53,831 --> 00:14:56,750
‎I told her to say we're close friends
‎because I was worried, all right?

242
00:14:57,835 --> 00:14:59,253
‎[sighs] Oh, man.

243
00:14:59,336 --> 00:15:01,088
‎Come on, Grandma.

244
00:15:01,171 --> 00:15:03,632
‎She's actually an amazing person.

245
00:15:05,718 --> 00:15:06,552
‎Well, fine.

246
00:15:07,636 --> 00:15:09,638
‎Okay. Go ahead.

247
00:15:09,722 --> 00:15:12,808
‎If you really like this woman,
‎then I have no intention of opposing it.

248
00:15:12,891 --> 00:15:14,184
‎R-Really?

249
00:15:14,268 --> 00:15:16,729
‎Sure, but I wanna take a look at it.

250
00:15:17,646 --> 00:15:19,314
‎-What?
‎-You're kidding, aren't you?

251
00:15:19,398 --> 00:15:21,900
‎I need her ‎saju‎, of course.
‎And her birth year sign too.

252
00:15:21,984 --> 00:15:24,945
‎Oh, come on! In this day and age?
‎Who cares about that stuff?

253
00:15:25,029 --> 00:15:27,197
‎That's the only thing I'm gonna check.

254
00:15:27,865 --> 00:15:30,367
‎Don't overreact. I just wanna look
‎at her ‎saju‎ and birth year sign.

255
00:15:30,451 --> 00:15:31,827
‎The only thing? That's everything!

256
00:15:32,786 --> 00:15:34,038
‎[groans]

257
00:15:34,121 --> 00:15:36,206
‎Hey, why are you so worried about it?

258
00:15:39,126 --> 00:15:41,670
‎Hold on, is there a chance her sign is…

259
00:15:42,755 --> 00:15:44,840
‎-Year of--
‎-No, what are you talking about? Come on.

260
00:15:45,966 --> 00:15:46,925
‎Then what?

261
00:15:48,052 --> 00:15:49,762
‎What is it? Monkey?

262
00:15:49,845 --> 00:15:52,806
‎Year of the Sheep. A White Sheep.

263
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:54,475
‎[exhales heavily]

264
00:15:56,602 --> 00:15:59,146
‎It's good. That is very good.

265
00:15:59,229 --> 00:16:02,941
‎-Ah, is it really?
‎-Sure. You couldn't ask for a better ‎saju‎.

266
00:16:03,025 --> 00:16:04,735
‎Perfect for a civil servant's wife.

267
00:16:04,818 --> 00:16:07,446
‎[laughing] Really?

268
00:16:07,529 --> 00:16:10,407
‎The husband will face
‎plenty of temptations from all around.

269
00:16:10,491 --> 00:16:12,451
‎And he'll be prone to being swayed.

270
00:16:12,534 --> 00:16:14,078
‎But her ‎saju‎ is so outstanding

271
00:16:14,161 --> 00:16:17,122
‎that her fortune as a wife
‎will smooth over everything.

272
00:16:17,206 --> 00:16:18,707
‎They should definitely go for it.

273
00:16:18,791 --> 00:16:23,462
‎Well, Gang-uk isn't like that at all.
‎He's not one to get swayed that easily.

274
00:16:23,545 --> 00:16:27,966
‎Then again, he's a prosecutor,
‎so he's bound to attract a lot of ladies.

275
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:29,885
‎I mean, it's part of the job,
‎ain't that right?

276
00:16:29,968 --> 00:16:31,345
‎[both chuckle]

277
00:16:31,428 --> 00:16:32,679
‎[exhales] Phew.

278
00:16:32,763 --> 00:16:35,015
‎Anyway, I'm really glad

279
00:16:36,266 --> 00:16:38,977
‎the two of them match. Whew.

280
00:16:39,061 --> 00:16:40,270
‎-Go ahead.
‎-Really?

281
00:16:40,354 --> 00:16:44,525
‎[panting] So you're saying
‎y-you're okay with it?

282
00:16:44,608 --> 00:16:48,362
‎Uh, in that case, I'll call you
‎as soon as we come up with a date.

283
00:16:48,445 --> 00:16:50,447
‎Uh-huh. Grandma, I love you!

284
00:16:50,531 --> 00:16:52,199
‎[kisses] See you!

285
00:16:53,117 --> 00:16:54,952
‎We're good. We did it, we're good.

286
00:16:55,911 --> 00:16:57,746
‎Man, I was so scared she'd figure it out.

287
00:16:57,830 --> 00:16:59,915
‎-[exhales]
‎-Wait, about the age thing?

288
00:16:59,998 --> 00:17:01,416
‎She's a year younger than my wife, right?

289
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:02,584
‎That's not gonna be a problem, is it?

290
00:17:02,668 --> 00:17:04,670
‎Nah, Grandma's not gonna ID her.
‎We're good.

291
00:17:04,753 --> 00:17:06,630
‎She'll just take
‎my word for it. It's fine.

292
00:17:06,713 --> 00:17:09,550
‎Seriously, how did you even think
‎to use his wife's ‎saju‎?

293
00:17:09,633 --> 00:17:12,094
‎Well, my grandma's really sharp,
‎you know that, right?

294
00:17:12,177 --> 00:17:15,556
‎If I gave her a fake one, she'd never
‎believe it, okay? So that's why I did it.

295
00:17:15,639 --> 00:17:17,057
‎[Ko] Yep. You're right about that.

296
00:17:17,141 --> 00:17:19,768
‎My mom went to
‎a fortune-teller too, actually.

297
00:17:19,852 --> 00:17:21,311
‎She wanted to check
‎my wife's ‎saju‎ before the wedding.

298
00:17:21,395 --> 00:17:23,105
‎-Uh-huh.
‎-And according to her reading,

299
00:17:23,188 --> 00:17:26,316
‎it's like she was destined
‎to marry someone like me,

300
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,235
‎-a civil servant.
‎-[Hyeong-min] Oh, wow.

301
00:17:28,318 --> 00:17:31,321
‎And I guess in a way, since Gang-uk and I
‎have so much in common,

302
00:17:31,405 --> 00:17:33,240
‎it makes sense we'd get a similar result.

303
00:17:33,824 --> 00:17:36,326
‎You have a lot in common? Give me
‎an example, what do you have in common?

304
00:17:36,410 --> 00:17:38,370
‎I shouldn't have to spell it out.

305
00:17:38,453 --> 00:17:41,707
‎And the fact that you're going
‎to make me do it is really annoying.

306
00:17:41,790 --> 00:17:43,917
‎-Okay. Civil servant, civil servant.
‎-Yeah.

307
00:17:44,001 --> 00:17:45,919
‎-He's good at his job.
‎-That's right.

308
00:17:46,003 --> 00:17:47,629
‎-I'm good at mine too, right?
‎-Uh-huh.

309
00:17:47,713 --> 00:17:49,047
‎And also, when it comes to looks…

310
00:17:49,131 --> 00:17:51,091
‎-Hey, that's enough!
‎-I didn't say anything.

311
00:17:51,175 --> 00:17:53,051
‎-Don't make me say it! Forget it.
‎-What do you mean? I didn't say anything.

312
00:17:53,135 --> 00:17:55,262
‎The only difference is,
‎he's a little younger.

313
00:17:55,345 --> 00:17:58,098
‎Just a little, but other than that,
‎we're both so, you know…

314
00:17:58,182 --> 00:18:00,809
‎-We're pretty much the same guy.
‎-Sure, sure. Absolutely. Uh-huh.

315
00:18:00,893 --> 00:18:02,519
‎Wow, you're really chatty today,
‎aren't you?

316
00:18:02,603 --> 00:18:03,478
‎Oh, come on.

317
00:18:03,562 --> 00:18:05,814
‎Gang-uk, does that mean
‎you're finally in the clear now?

318
00:18:05,898 --> 00:18:07,024
‎No more obstacles?

319
00:18:07,107 --> 00:18:08,483
‎That's right, I'm all clear.

320
00:18:08,567 --> 00:18:09,860
‎No obstacles.

321
00:18:10,944 --> 00:18:12,154
‎You wanna meet his family?

322
00:18:12,237 --> 00:18:16,116
‎Of course. It's only right
‎that we meet before the ceremony.

323
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,994
‎Gang-uk said his grandmother
‎is his only family left, right?

324
00:18:19,077 --> 00:18:19,912
‎Should be easy.

325
00:18:20,704 --> 00:18:23,373
‎I'm sorry, Gang-uk.
‎I keep throwing curveballs at you.

326
00:18:23,457 --> 00:18:24,917
‎Oh, no, don't worry, not at all.

327
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,669
‎Uh, funny enough,
‎my grandma said she wanted to do that too.

328
00:18:28,712 --> 00:18:31,965
‎How about I just bring her
‎to Reina next Wednesday? How's that?

329
00:18:32,049 --> 00:18:34,676
‎-[chuckles] Great.
‎-Yeo-ri.

330
00:18:35,344 --> 00:18:38,513
‎If we're going through the motions anyway,
‎why not enjoy it, you know?

331
00:18:40,224 --> 00:18:42,476
‎Agreed. [chuckles]

332
00:18:42,559 --> 00:18:44,061
‎See you on Wednesday.

333
00:18:44,728 --> 00:18:45,562
‎Okay.

334
00:18:50,525 --> 00:18:51,526
‎[elevator bell dings]

335
00:18:51,610 --> 00:18:53,528
‎-That lady in the woolen dress?
‎-Yeah!

336
00:18:53,612 --> 00:18:55,072
‎-She's so simple--
‎-I just--

337
00:18:55,155 --> 00:18:56,990
‎-Uh, hello, ma'am.
‎-Hello.

338
00:19:03,997 --> 00:19:05,415
‎-Come on in.
‎-Sorry?

339
00:19:05,499 --> 00:19:06,333
‎Thank you so much.

340
00:19:07,542 --> 00:19:08,627
‎Thank you.

341
00:19:15,467 --> 00:19:17,761
‎[quirky music playing]

342
00:19:25,352 --> 00:19:27,020
‎[elevator bell dings]

343
00:19:29,064 --> 00:19:31,066
‎[both] Have a good day.

344
00:19:34,111 --> 00:19:35,404
‎Keep up the good work.

345
00:19:36,071 --> 00:19:37,364
‎-Oh…
‎-Sure.

346
00:19:39,992 --> 00:19:42,035
‎-Whoa!
‎-She's not like the rumors said.

347
00:19:42,119 --> 00:19:43,161
‎I know, right?

348
00:19:43,245 --> 00:19:45,455
‎I also thought
‎she's even prettier up close, right?

349
00:19:45,539 --> 00:19:46,415
‎Yeah, she is.

350
00:19:47,582 --> 00:19:49,459
‎[Ms. Eom] Oh, wow. Matching rings?

351
00:19:49,543 --> 00:19:51,753
‎[employee]
‎Actually, it's an engagement ring.

352
00:19:51,837 --> 00:19:53,005
‎He proposed yesterday.

353
00:19:53,922 --> 00:19:57,259
‎He asked me out to dinner, then suddenly
‎he said he wanted to go for a walk.

354
00:19:57,342 --> 00:20:00,512
‎I wasn't expecting anything,
‎but then we sat down on a bench

355
00:20:01,221 --> 00:20:03,348
‎and he suddenly got down
‎on one knee with a ring.

356
00:20:03,432 --> 00:20:05,434
‎[Ms. Eom] Aw… That's so nice.

357
00:20:05,517 --> 00:20:07,185
‎[employee]
‎How was it when you got engaged?

358
00:20:07,269 --> 00:20:10,480
‎Me? [grunts] Ice cream surprise.

359
00:20:10,564 --> 00:20:11,565
‎[both chuckle]

360
00:20:11,648 --> 00:20:13,525
‎[Ms. Eom] He hid the ring in there.
‎I almost swallowed it.

361
00:20:13,608 --> 00:20:14,776
‎[employee] You should've swallowed it.

362
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:16,528
‎-[Ms. Eom] I should have.
‎-[employee laughs]

363
00:20:19,114 --> 00:20:21,158
‎-[phone buzzing]
‎-I've got it, I've got it.

364
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,577
‎Uh, hello, hello?

365
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,245
‎Hey, Grandma.
‎I was supposed to pick you up.

366
00:20:25,329 --> 00:20:27,956
‎Um, I'm sorry. Something came up
‎in a case I had to wrap up.

367
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:30,250
‎Goodness, what are you talking about?

368
00:20:30,334 --> 00:20:33,420
‎Serving the country comes first. [laughs]

369
00:20:33,503 --> 00:20:35,297
‎I'm already at Reina, it's all right.

370
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:36,423
‎You take your time, okay?

371
00:20:36,506 --> 00:20:38,300
‎What? You're already there?

372
00:20:38,383 --> 00:20:40,218
‎[stammers] Okay, I'll be there
‎as soon as I can.

373
00:20:40,302 --> 00:20:42,512
‎Sure. Okay. [chuckles]

374
00:20:44,556 --> 00:20:45,891
‎[sighs]

375
00:20:45,974 --> 00:20:50,771
‎So this is where my future
‎granddaughter-in-law works. [sighs]

376
00:20:51,563 --> 00:20:54,316
‎Everything's ready.
‎The room looks simple yet elegant,

377
00:20:54,399 --> 00:20:55,984
‎just as you requested, ma'am.

378
00:20:56,068 --> 00:20:59,905
‎I've also had the kitchen prepare a meal
‎tailored for an elderly guest.

379
00:20:59,988 --> 00:21:00,989
‎-[chuckles]
‎-Yeah.

380
00:21:01,990 --> 00:21:04,284
‎[gasps] Oh, no. I forgot my medicine.

381
00:21:04,368 --> 00:21:06,745
‎I'll get it for you.
‎I'll leave it at the meeting room.

382
00:21:06,828 --> 00:21:08,413
‎[chuckles]

383
00:21:10,332 --> 00:21:11,166
‎[groans]

384
00:21:14,086 --> 00:21:14,920
‎Oh!

385
00:21:16,171 --> 00:21:17,422
‎Are you feeling unwell?

386
00:21:17,506 --> 00:21:18,840
‎Oh, no. I'm okay. It's fine.

387
00:21:18,924 --> 00:21:21,843
‎We wouldn't want you to pass out
‎and fall. You could get hurt. Come on.

388
00:21:21,927 --> 00:21:24,554
‎Lean on me, let's go.
‎Let's sit you down over there.

389
00:21:24,638 --> 00:21:26,348
‎Okay? Here.

390
00:21:26,431 --> 00:21:27,432
‎-[whimpers]
‎-Oh, my!

391
00:21:27,516 --> 00:21:30,519
‎You've got some heavy bones.
‎You're heavier than I expected.

392
00:21:30,602 --> 00:21:32,145
‎[phone buzzing]

393
00:21:33,021 --> 00:21:34,022
‎Yes?

394
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:38,652
‎Ah, is that so?
‎I'll be right down. Thank you. Bye.

395
00:21:42,447 --> 00:21:44,449
‎-[Baek groaning]
‎-[gasps]

396
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:46,910
‎Goodness, you look pale.
‎You don't look well at all.

397
00:21:46,993 --> 00:21:49,788
‎I should call an ambulance for you,
‎shouldn't I?

398
00:21:49,871 --> 00:21:52,749
‎No, I'm just gonna rest a little
‎and I'll be fine. Thanks, ma'am.

399
00:21:52,833 --> 00:21:54,209
‎Mm-hmm.

400
00:21:54,292 --> 00:21:55,293
‎-[sighs]
‎-[phone buzzing]

401
00:21:55,377 --> 00:21:56,253
‎Oh?

402
00:21:57,295 --> 00:21:58,713
‎INCOMING CALL
‎MY GANG-UK

403
00:21:58,797 --> 00:22:00,006
‎[laughs]

404
00:22:00,799 --> 00:22:03,009
‎Huh? Hi!

405
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,011
‎Uh-huh.

406
00:22:05,095 --> 00:22:06,513
‎Yeah, the front, the front.

407
00:22:06,596 --> 00:22:09,433
‎Actually, at the lobby.
‎Sitting down at the lobby, yeah.

408
00:22:09,516 --> 00:22:11,643
‎Ah, your girlfriend's already here?

409
00:22:11,726 --> 00:22:14,187
‎-[laughs] Okay, okay. Yeah, I got it.
‎-[sighs]

410
00:22:14,271 --> 00:22:16,106
‎I'll just stay put. I'll wait here.

411
00:22:16,189 --> 00:22:17,941
‎Okay! Yeah.

412
00:22:18,024 --> 00:22:19,151
‎[chuckles]

413
00:22:20,485 --> 00:22:21,653
‎All right.

414
00:22:21,736 --> 00:22:24,739
‎You know, I'm here to meet
‎my future granddaughter-in-law, actually.

415
00:22:24,823 --> 00:22:28,034
‎-Ah.
‎-Nice, right? What about you?

416
00:22:28,118 --> 00:22:29,911
‎-Yeah, me too.
‎-Oh, ah!

417
00:22:29,995 --> 00:22:31,997
‎-You're meeting your granddaughter-in-law?
‎-Grandson.

418
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,582
‎Future grandson-in-law.

419
00:22:33,665 --> 00:22:37,419
‎Ah! Such a fun coincidence, huh?

420
00:22:37,502 --> 00:22:39,171
‎[both chuckle]

421
00:22:39,254 --> 00:22:44,301
‎My future granddaughter-in-law
‎works here too, at the Reina Hotel.

422
00:22:44,384 --> 00:22:45,427
‎Oh, wow.

423
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:46,720
‎Which department? Do you know?

424
00:22:46,803 --> 00:22:48,388
‎I couldn't tell you that. I'm not sure.

425
00:22:48,471 --> 00:22:51,183
‎All I know is, she's a proper girl.

426
00:22:51,266 --> 00:22:54,102
‎The fortune says she'd make
‎an ideal wife for a civil servant.

427
00:22:54,186 --> 00:22:56,938
‎The type who'll support her husband
‎and keep the house running.

428
00:22:57,022 --> 00:22:58,607
‎A devoted wife, I just love it.

429
00:22:58,690 --> 00:23:01,276
‎[chuckles] How about in your case?

430
00:23:02,068 --> 00:23:04,154
‎Does it look like they'll be a good match?

431
00:23:04,237 --> 00:23:05,614
‎Sure, I guess.

432
00:23:05,697 --> 00:23:08,074
‎-Ah!
‎-Well…

433
00:23:08,742 --> 00:23:11,328
‎I'm not worried.
‎He's supportive, and he cheers her on.

434
00:23:11,411 --> 00:23:12,913
‎-They seem like a good fit.
‎-Ah.

435
00:23:12,996 --> 00:23:13,872
‎[both chuckle]

436
00:23:13,955 --> 00:23:18,460
‎As long as he's not just riding
‎on her success.

437
00:23:18,543 --> 00:23:21,463
‎Oh! So she's successful then?

438
00:23:21,546 --> 00:23:22,797
‎Mm-hmm.

439
00:23:23,548 --> 00:23:27,552
‎Women are getting careers now,
‎making money, times have changed, right?

440
00:23:27,636 --> 00:23:30,764
‎You must be so proud of her,
‎congratulations.

441
00:23:30,847 --> 00:23:33,099
‎Yeah. And same goes for you, too.

442
00:23:33,183 --> 00:23:36,728
‎-Ah, yes, yes, absolutely, I'm proud.
‎-[Gang-uk] Oh!

443
00:23:36,811 --> 00:23:39,064
‎-[Gang-uk, Yeo-ri] Grandma!
‎-Oh?

444
00:23:40,941 --> 00:23:41,858
‎Huh?

445
00:23:46,321 --> 00:23:47,906
‎[sighs]

446
00:23:49,074 --> 00:23:51,743
‎-Hmm.
‎-So, this is my grandmother, Mrs. Pang.

447
00:23:51,826 --> 00:23:52,911
‎Uh-huh.

448
00:23:53,495 --> 00:23:55,538
‎This is my grandmother, Mrs. Baek.

449
00:23:56,248 --> 00:24:00,460
‎[sighs] You know, thinking about it,
‎maybe fate brought us together earlier.

450
00:24:00,543 --> 00:24:03,004
‎-Don't you think? [chuckles]
‎-Yes, who knows?

451
00:24:03,630 --> 00:24:06,132
‎Your granddaughter's great.
‎I'm happy about this engagement.

452
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:09,219
‎I had their compatibility checked,
‎and they're a good match.

453
00:24:09,302 --> 00:24:11,888
‎I'm someone who believes in ‎saju‎,
‎so I had to check.

454
00:24:11,972 --> 00:24:14,683
‎Everything seemed pretty favorable.

455
00:24:14,766 --> 00:24:16,559
‎With him being born
‎in the Year of the Horse, and her--

456
00:24:16,643 --> 00:24:17,894
‎-[all gasp]
‎-[coughing]

457
00:24:17,978 --> 00:24:19,688
‎-What's going on?
‎-Are you…

458
00:24:21,273 --> 00:24:22,148
‎Are you all right?

459
00:24:22,232 --> 00:24:25,193
‎Uh, yeah. It went down the wrong pipe.
‎I'm… I'm sorry.

460
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:27,696
‎-Hey, are you sure?
‎-I'm sure.

461
00:24:27,779 --> 00:24:28,989
‎[chuckles]

462
00:24:29,072 --> 00:24:33,910
‎So, Mrs. Baek. Do you also care about ‎saju
‎and compatibility?

463
00:24:33,994 --> 00:24:35,662
‎Do I care about it?

464
00:24:35,745 --> 00:24:37,455
‎Oh! Yes, absolutely.

465
00:24:37,539 --> 00:24:40,375
‎[chuckles] I just didn't bother this time.

466
00:24:41,251 --> 00:24:44,796
‎They're already set on getting engaged,
‎so I spared myself the frustration.

467
00:24:44,879 --> 00:24:46,756
‎Besides, they're not kids, right?

468
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:48,717
‎So I decided to respect their wishes.

469
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:51,553
‎[chuckles] Yeah, yeah,
‎but you wouldn't be frustrated,

470
00:24:51,636 --> 00:24:54,597
‎because my ‎saju ‎reader
‎says they're a great match.

471
00:24:54,681 --> 00:24:58,518
‎[chuckles] But, um,
‎there's something I wanted to clarify.

472
00:24:58,601 --> 00:25:01,604
‎That thing you said earlier,
‎you didn't mean that, right?

473
00:25:04,190 --> 00:25:06,526
‎The "riding on her success" thing.

474
00:25:06,609 --> 00:25:08,653
‎I don't know if you know this,

475
00:25:08,737 --> 00:25:09,863
‎but Gang-uk here?

476
00:25:09,946 --> 00:25:12,824
‎He went to Korea's number one university.

477
00:25:12,907 --> 00:25:14,492
‎He got in straight out of high school,

478
00:25:14,576 --> 00:25:17,746
‎and then he passed
‎the bar exam on his first try,

479
00:25:17,829 --> 00:25:19,247
‎before he even graduated.

480
00:25:19,331 --> 00:25:21,958
‎What do you call it? He's a total protégé!

481
00:25:22,042 --> 00:25:23,835
‎That's not it. A total prodigy.

482
00:25:23,918 --> 00:25:27,756
‎Gang-uk is a prodigy. He passed the exam
‎before he even graduated.

483
00:25:27,839 --> 00:25:32,844
‎So earlier, when you said that thing
‎about riding on her success, wow.

484
00:25:32,927 --> 00:25:35,388
‎That got me thinking, "Nah!
‎That is never going to be his case."

485
00:25:35,472 --> 00:25:37,974
‎-Grandma, can you stop?
‎-Leave me alone.

486
00:25:38,058 --> 00:25:40,268
‎So yeah. That's what I wanted to say.

487
00:25:40,352 --> 00:25:45,398
‎Okay. [chuckles] Earlier,
‎you said something about a "devoted wife"?

488
00:25:45,482 --> 00:25:48,610
‎Well, the world
‎doesn't work like that anymore.

489
00:25:48,693 --> 00:25:50,195
‎I don't know how to explain it.

490
00:25:50,278 --> 00:25:53,740
‎You see, she had to drop out
‎of high school, actually,

491
00:25:53,823 --> 00:25:57,410
‎because of some personal issues,
‎but she still got into Wharton.

492
00:25:57,494 --> 00:26:01,247
‎The number one global MBA program
‎in the US. Wharton.

493
00:26:01,831 --> 00:26:05,377
‎Getting in was an absolute breeze
‎for a prodigy like her.

494
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:08,338
‎-Right now she's only running this hotel.
‎-What's she talking about?

495
00:26:08,421 --> 00:26:11,049
‎But our goal is to get her to oversee

496
00:26:11,132 --> 00:26:13,551
‎the entirety of the Reina Group
‎in the near future.

497
00:26:13,635 --> 00:26:16,971
‎Which is why she a needs husband
‎who can stand behind her.

498
00:26:17,055 --> 00:26:19,599
‎[groans] Stand behind her? Please.

499
00:26:19,682 --> 00:26:22,102
‎It's not like he doesn't have
‎anything better to do.

500
00:26:22,185 --> 00:26:26,147
‎He's a busy man, he has a lot on his
‎plate. He's not gonna stand behind anyone.

501
00:26:26,231 --> 00:26:28,525
‎Gang-uk, is that really the case?

502
00:26:28,608 --> 00:26:30,693
‎No. I'll always stand behind her.

503
00:26:30,777 --> 00:26:32,237
‎[tense, quirky music playing]

504
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:33,571
‎Can you relax?

505
00:26:34,322 --> 00:26:35,365
‎Oh…

506
00:26:36,241 --> 00:26:39,202
‎[stammers]
‎Of course I'll also stand behind him.

507
00:26:39,285 --> 00:26:40,745
‎You remember, don't you?

508
00:26:40,829 --> 00:26:42,497
‎I'll open the gate for you.

509
00:26:44,874 --> 00:26:46,042
‎[gasps]

510
00:26:46,126 --> 00:26:48,336
‎I would do anything to support him.

511
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:50,964
‎No matter what, whatever it takes.

512
00:26:51,047 --> 00:26:53,091
‎-[Madam Pang] Huh.
‎-Isn't that what a devoted wife does,

513
00:26:53,174 --> 00:26:54,259
‎Mrs. Pang?

514
00:26:56,094 --> 00:26:59,347
‎Something, just…
‎Something feels off right now.

515
00:26:59,431 --> 00:27:01,349
‎Grandma, why'd
‎you have to make things awkward?

516
00:27:01,433 --> 00:27:03,560
‎Well, she started it.
‎She's the one who brought up nonsense

517
00:27:03,643 --> 00:27:05,562
‎about men riding
‎on her granddaughter's success.

518
00:27:05,645 --> 00:27:08,064
‎I can't watch you end up living
‎under someone else's thumb.

519
00:27:08,148 --> 00:27:11,443
‎Yeah, well, still, I've already made up
‎my mind. Why do you even care?

520
00:27:11,526 --> 00:27:12,569
‎[sighs]

521
00:27:13,695 --> 00:27:15,947
‎[groans] Why did you lie to me?

522
00:27:17,073 --> 00:27:19,033
‎This girl owns a bunch of motels…

523
00:27:19,117 --> 00:27:21,578
‎Sorry, hotels, and she's a CEO?
‎She's a ‎chaebol‎. She's super rich.

524
00:27:21,661 --> 00:27:24,998
‎Grandma, I didn't lie.
‎I just omitted a thing or two.

525
00:27:25,081 --> 00:27:27,750
‎And what difference does it make?
‎I don't care about any of that.

526
00:27:27,834 --> 00:27:29,794
‎I'm in it because of who she is,
‎not what she has.

527
00:27:29,878 --> 00:27:30,712
‎Trust me.

528
00:27:31,296 --> 00:27:34,132
‎I'd rather you married
‎a simple woman from a simple family,

529
00:27:34,215 --> 00:27:37,051
‎-not a rich, cocky boss lady.
‎-Yeo-ri's not like that.

530
00:27:37,135 --> 00:27:39,637
‎Other than being beautiful,
‎she's completely unassuming.

531
00:27:39,721 --> 00:27:41,431
‎She's not cocky at all.

532
00:27:41,514 --> 00:27:43,016
‎And hold on a second there.

533
00:27:43,099 --> 00:27:45,018
‎Come on, you said you were happy for me.

534
00:27:45,101 --> 00:27:47,061
‎You said you liked her ‎saju.
‎Why the change?

535
00:27:47,979 --> 00:27:48,855
‎That's right.

536
00:27:48,938 --> 00:27:51,566
‎You've got a point.
‎Shaman Shim must've read her ‎saju‎ wrong.

537
00:27:51,649 --> 00:27:53,943
‎My goodness! He was way off.

538
00:27:54,027 --> 00:27:55,069
‎[groans]

539
00:27:55,153 --> 00:27:56,738
‎-I'll give him a piece of my mind.
‎-Grandma. Wait a minute.

540
00:27:57,822 --> 00:28:00,200
‎Hey. Listen to me,
‎I really want you to like Yeo-ri.

541
00:28:00,283 --> 00:28:02,577
‎That would really make me happy, huh?

542
00:28:03,244 --> 00:28:04,370
‎Come on.

543
00:28:04,454 --> 00:28:06,122
‎Oh, you sweet little thing.

544
00:28:06,206 --> 00:28:07,874
‎[laughs] You really like her that much?

545
00:28:07,957 --> 00:28:09,083
‎Mm-hmm. I like her a lot.

546
00:28:09,667 --> 00:28:11,377
‎Oh, my sweet boy…

547
00:28:12,086 --> 00:28:14,255
‎Oh, what can I say?

548
00:28:16,508 --> 00:28:17,759
‎Fine.

549
00:28:18,968 --> 00:28:21,304
‎But never forget I've got your back, okay?

550
00:28:21,387 --> 00:28:24,057
‎Don't ever let them push you around.

551
00:28:24,140 --> 00:28:25,850
‎-Okay?
‎-Goes without saying.

552
00:28:25,934 --> 00:28:28,645
‎I'm your grandson, aren't I? Yeah!

553
00:28:28,728 --> 00:28:29,729
‎[both grunt]

554
00:28:29,812 --> 00:28:31,147
‎[Gang-uk] ‎Now I'm completely in the clear.

555
00:28:31,231 --> 00:28:33,024
‎-Cheers. Cheers.
‎-[Hyeong-min] Oh!

556
00:28:33,983 --> 00:28:36,027
‎So, the whole ‎saju‎ thing worked out?

557
00:28:36,110 --> 00:28:37,111
‎[Gang-uk] Mmm…

558
00:28:37,820 --> 00:28:38,947
‎Kinda.

559
00:28:39,030 --> 00:28:40,782
‎They started bragging
‎about their grandkids, it was…

560
00:28:40,865 --> 00:28:42,116
‎-Well, you know.
‎-[Hyeong-min] Oh!

561
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:44,035
‎Goes to show, you shouldn't
‎lie to your grandma.

562
00:28:44,118 --> 00:28:45,829
‎-Mm-hmm.
‎-You reap what you sow.

563
00:28:46,412 --> 00:28:48,206
‎Wait, but what happens if she finds out?

564
00:28:48,289 --> 00:28:50,291
‎-You need a contingency plan, right?
‎-Not really.

565
00:28:50,375 --> 00:28:52,877
‎I'm taking it one day at the time,
‎or I'll go crazy.

566
00:28:52,961 --> 00:28:54,003
‎Yeah, you do that.

567
00:28:54,629 --> 00:28:55,839
‎Cross that bridge when you get to it.

568
00:28:56,589 --> 00:28:58,550
‎Your family was
‎against your marriage too, right?

569
00:28:58,633 --> 00:29:00,176
‎-Yeah, they were a little against it.
‎-Thanks.

570
00:29:00,260 --> 00:29:02,053
‎I thought they were really against it.

571
00:29:02,136 --> 00:29:03,763
‎I wouldn't say
‎they were really against it,

572
00:29:03,847 --> 00:29:06,307
‎because, like I told you,
‎it was just the age gap.

573
00:29:06,391 --> 00:29:09,185
‎But sooner or later, people can tell
‎I'm a solid man.

574
00:29:09,269 --> 00:29:11,563
‎I'm the real deal. Anyone can tell.

575
00:29:11,646 --> 00:29:14,482
‎[Yeo-ri] ‎I'm doing this for your own good,
‎to protect you.

576
00:29:14,566 --> 00:29:16,901
‎We're setting up boundaries ahead of time.

577
00:29:16,985 --> 00:29:19,404
‎I thought, even if it's just once,

578
00:29:19,487 --> 00:29:23,741
‎I'd like to go out and have myself a drink
‎around a crowd of people. That's all.

579
00:29:23,825 --> 00:29:25,660
‎[Hyeong-min] Hmm. If you say so.

580
00:29:25,743 --> 00:29:28,746
‎Why are you always finding excuses
‎not to go home? Your wife's beautiful.

581
00:29:29,831 --> 00:29:32,959
‎Well, I'll put it this way.
‎Looks aren't everything.

582
00:29:33,042 --> 00:29:35,253
‎-[coughing]
‎-[laughs]

583
00:29:37,255 --> 00:29:40,341
‎Hello? Yeo-ri, have you eaten yet?

584
00:29:40,425 --> 00:29:42,552
‎[grunts] No, not yet.

585
00:29:43,845 --> 00:29:46,014
‎-What about you?
‎-Oh, I was just…

586
00:29:46,097 --> 00:29:47,223
‎[gentle, romantic music playing]

587
00:29:47,307 --> 00:29:48,558
‎You're at the restaurant.

588
00:29:49,601 --> 00:29:51,060
‎How are Pil-dong and Hyeong-min?

589
00:29:51,144 --> 00:29:52,145
‎Are they doing all right?

590
00:29:52,228 --> 00:29:53,354
‎They are.

591
00:29:54,647 --> 00:29:58,276
‎Yeo-ri, listen, we've done a bunch
‎of the usual date things already.

592
00:29:58,359 --> 00:30:00,361
‎But I was thinking,
‎and if I'm not mistaken,

593
00:30:00,445 --> 00:30:02,196
‎we haven't had
‎many meals together, have we?

594
00:30:02,822 --> 00:30:04,282
‎-Oh, you're right.
‎-Right?

595
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:08,620
‎In fact, Hyeong-min was talking about
‎this new spot everyone's talking about.

596
00:30:08,703 --> 00:30:10,246
‎He said I should take you.

597
00:30:10,330 --> 00:30:11,956
‎So… are you free tomorrow?

598
00:30:12,040 --> 00:30:13,082
‎Sure.

599
00:30:18,379 --> 00:30:21,674
‎Uh, so where is this new spot
‎he mentioned exactly?

600
00:30:21,758 --> 00:30:24,928
‎Huh? Oh. It's, uh…

601
00:30:25,929 --> 00:30:28,264
‎I'll get the details from Hyeong-min
‎and I'll send them to you.

602
00:30:29,474 --> 00:30:31,142
‎Oh, and actually,

603
00:30:31,225 --> 00:30:34,145
‎there's something I need to take care of
‎before we get engaged.

604
00:30:35,063 --> 00:30:35,939
‎Oh, what is it?

605
00:30:36,606 --> 00:30:38,358
‎Wait until tomorrow. You'll find out.

606
00:30:39,859 --> 00:30:42,153
‎Sounds good. So I'll see you tomorrow.

607
00:30:42,236 --> 00:30:43,488
‎Bye.

608
00:30:46,658 --> 00:30:48,201
‎-[Hyeong-min] It's not bad.
‎-[Gang-uk] Hyeong-min.

609
00:30:48,284 --> 00:30:49,661
‎-It's supposed to be good.
‎-That's it, not bad.

610
00:30:49,744 --> 00:30:51,663
‎Hey, Hyeong-min.
‎I need a trendy new spot to eat.

611
00:30:51,746 --> 00:30:52,914
‎-Just give me a list.
‎-Trendy and new?

612
00:30:52,997 --> 00:30:54,624
‎-Uh-huh.
‎-We're going for a second round?

613
00:30:54,707 --> 00:30:56,167
‎Nah, of course not. Just tell me, come on.

614
00:30:57,752 --> 00:30:59,545
‎He's so secretive.

615
00:30:59,629 --> 00:31:02,590
‎What would he need to do
‎before getting engaged?

616
00:31:02,674 --> 00:31:04,300
‎[ghostly hissing]

617
00:31:06,219 --> 00:31:07,220
‎Huh?

618
00:31:07,303 --> 00:31:10,098
‎[scoffs] He's proposing with a ring?

619
00:31:10,765 --> 00:31:12,475
‎No way, come on.

620
00:31:16,187 --> 00:31:18,439
‎The ceremony's coming up soon…

621
00:31:19,565 --> 00:31:21,234
‎I guess a ring

622
00:31:22,110 --> 00:31:24,320
‎is something I need after all.

623
00:31:24,404 --> 00:31:26,656
‎[ghostly hissing]

624
00:31:28,491 --> 00:31:29,867
‎[chuckles]

625
00:31:30,743 --> 00:31:32,662
‎[upbeat music playing]

626
00:31:51,597 --> 00:31:53,307
‎Ugh. This one doesn't feel right either.

627
00:32:30,094 --> 00:32:30,928
‎Yeo-ri.

628
00:32:46,152 --> 00:32:49,614
‎This is where Cha Hyeon-u,
‎the soccer player, proposed to his wife.

629
00:32:49,697 --> 00:32:51,991
‎[quirky music playing]

630
00:32:52,075 --> 00:32:52,909
‎Ah.

631
00:32:54,619 --> 00:32:55,953
‎Here are your desserts.

632
00:32:56,037 --> 00:32:57,246
‎Thank you.

633
00:32:58,164 --> 00:33:00,958
‎-[employee] ‎An engagement ring.
‎-[Ms. Eom] ‎Ice cream surprise.

634
00:33:01,042 --> 00:33:03,252
‎He hid in the ring in there.
‎I almost swallowed it.

635
00:33:24,732 --> 00:33:25,691
‎It's weird.

636
00:33:25,775 --> 00:33:28,236
‎Apparently, he hid the ring
‎inside the ice cream.

637
00:33:28,778 --> 00:33:32,073
‎Is that still the way
‎people do it these days?

638
00:33:32,156 --> 00:33:34,534
‎[coughing]

639
00:33:40,498 --> 00:33:42,625
‎-Are you okay?
‎-Yeah.

640
00:33:44,293 --> 00:33:46,629
‎Uh, Yeo-ri,
‎once we're done with our meals,

641
00:33:46,712 --> 00:33:47,922
‎why don't we go for a walk?

642
00:33:48,005 --> 00:33:49,298
‎The weather's nice.

643
00:33:50,007 --> 00:33:51,676
‎-A walk? Right now?
‎-Mm-hmm.

644
00:33:51,759 --> 00:33:53,386
‎[employee] ‎He asked me out to dinner,
‎then suddenly he said

645
00:33:53,469 --> 00:33:55,388
‎-he wanted to go for a walk.
‎-[Ms. Eom] ‎Mm-hmm.

646
00:33:58,307 --> 00:34:01,978
‎-Wow, they're in full bloom.
‎-Mm-hmm. Yeah, they are.

647
00:34:02,603 --> 00:34:03,437
‎So pretty.

648
00:34:05,731 --> 00:34:08,943
‎[employee] ‎I wasn't expecting anything,
‎but then we sat down on a bench

649
00:34:09,026 --> 00:34:11,612
‎and he suddenly got down
‎on one knee with a ring.

650
00:34:12,530 --> 00:34:13,781
‎Just a moment, Yeo-ri.

651
00:34:14,448 --> 00:34:16,367
‎Oh, my gosh! Here? Out of nowhere?

652
00:34:21,706 --> 00:34:24,500
‎[Gang-uk] I got something on my shoe. Ugh.

653
00:34:25,042 --> 00:34:26,669
‎[chuckles weakly] That's bad.

654
00:34:28,462 --> 00:34:29,630
‎There, all done.

655
00:34:30,214 --> 00:34:32,508
‎-I'm glad.
‎-[chuckles]

656
00:34:33,176 --> 00:34:34,135
‎Mmm…

657
00:34:36,679 --> 00:34:37,680
‎Do your feet hurt?

658
00:34:38,556 --> 00:34:40,099
‎-No, I'm fine.
‎-Hmm.

659
00:34:42,143 --> 00:34:43,603
‎What if we sat down over there?

660
00:34:45,146 --> 00:34:46,063
‎Okay.

661
00:34:49,442 --> 00:34:50,610
‎-Right here?
‎-Yeah.

662
00:34:51,944 --> 00:34:53,446
‎Yeo-ri, hold on.

663
00:34:56,240 --> 00:34:58,951
‎-You can use this if you want.
‎-Oh. Thank you.

664
00:35:05,625 --> 00:35:07,627
‎Are you not going to sit down?

665
00:35:07,710 --> 00:35:08,753
‎Um…

666
00:35:10,796 --> 00:35:12,048
‎Why? What's going on?

667
00:35:12,965 --> 00:35:15,593
‎I know this might come across as a lot,

668
00:35:16,469 --> 00:35:19,805
‎but there's something I wanna give you
‎before we get engaged.

669
00:35:21,474 --> 00:35:24,143
‎Uh… What is it?

670
00:35:24,227 --> 00:35:26,103
‎Would you mind waiting here for a bit?
‎It's in the car.

671
00:35:26,187 --> 00:35:27,647
‎I'll go grab it and be back in a second.

672
00:35:27,730 --> 00:35:30,775
‎-I'll be quick.
‎-Oh. Uh… It's okay, take your time.

673
00:35:30,858 --> 00:35:32,485
‎[romantic music playing]

674
00:36:27,373 --> 00:36:30,543
‎Oh. My goodness,
‎you keep getting down on your knees.

675
00:36:33,421 --> 00:36:34,463
‎Yeo-ri.

676
00:36:52,857 --> 00:36:54,275
‎[music fades]

677
00:37:02,366 --> 00:37:03,576
‎The acupuncture needle? Wh…

678
00:37:05,870 --> 00:37:07,997
‎Why is this… No, wait.

679
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:09,123
‎This wasn't what…

680
00:37:10,041 --> 00:37:11,208
‎-[groans]
‎-Sorry, but I should go.

681
00:37:12,251 --> 00:37:14,003
‎Wait a minute. I didn't…

682
00:37:17,757 --> 00:37:20,259
‎Wait. Wait a minute, Yeo-ri.

683
00:37:20,343 --> 00:37:22,636
‎-Yeo-ri, wait, don't go. Yeo-ri!
‎-[panting]

684
00:37:22,720 --> 00:37:24,638
‎Exactly, I know.

685
00:37:25,222 --> 00:37:28,142
‎Why did it have to be shaped
‎just like a ring box?

686
00:37:28,225 --> 00:37:30,227
‎It was bound to cause confusion. I get it.

687
00:37:31,312 --> 00:37:33,898
‎[sighs] Oh, I'm so embarrassed.

688
00:37:35,858 --> 00:37:37,026
‎[ghostly hissing]

689
00:37:37,109 --> 00:37:39,445
‎No, I'm not upset at you
‎or anything like that.

690
00:37:39,528 --> 00:37:42,490
‎I'm just feeling embarrassed, that's all.

691
00:37:42,573 --> 00:37:44,575
‎I can't believe I thought he'd--

692
00:37:46,494 --> 00:37:48,537
‎Our engagement is right around the corner.

693
00:37:49,580 --> 00:37:51,791
‎I got my hopes up without realizing it.

694
00:37:53,376 --> 00:37:55,961
‎-[scoffs]
‎-[ghostly hissing]

695
00:37:57,963 --> 00:37:59,965
‎Is that a matching ring?

696
00:38:01,717 --> 00:38:03,469
‎[giggles]

697
00:38:03,552 --> 00:38:05,971
‎Hmm. It's really nice.

698
00:38:07,056 --> 00:38:08,516
‎Bet it feels nice.

699
00:38:08,599 --> 00:38:11,102
‎[groans]
‎I can't believe I got the wrong one.

700
00:38:16,482 --> 00:38:18,109
‎-Oh, my!
‎-Hey, shut up. Just a second.

701
00:38:18,192 --> 00:38:20,236
‎-Oh!
‎-[laughing]

702
00:38:20,319 --> 00:38:22,363
‎-I can't wait to marry you, sweetheart.
‎-[Gang-uk groans]

703
00:38:22,446 --> 00:38:23,864
‎Help me keep his hand still, come on.

704
00:38:23,948 --> 00:38:26,075
‎Wait, is there a reason
‎you're not supposed to touch her hand?

705
00:38:26,158 --> 00:38:29,954
‎Hey, come on. Of course there's a reason.
‎Can you just focus? Stay still.

706
00:38:30,037 --> 00:38:31,914
‎-Don't move, Pil-dong.
‎-You're so grumpy today, honey.

707
00:38:31,997 --> 00:38:33,082
‎Can you not do that?

708
00:38:34,291 --> 00:38:36,085
‎Almost. Almost, almost.

709
00:38:36,961 --> 00:38:37,795
‎[whimpers]

710
00:38:39,630 --> 00:38:43,050
‎[groans] All that practicing
‎with the guys, all for nothing.

711
00:38:45,386 --> 00:38:47,430
‎[groans] I can't believe it.

712
00:38:47,513 --> 00:38:49,014
‎[groaning]

713
00:38:54,311 --> 00:38:55,980
‎Hui-won, how are you?

714
00:38:56,063 --> 00:38:57,648
‎This is Gang-uk's grandmother.

715
00:38:57,731 --> 00:39:00,943
‎Mrs. Pang, hi! How's everything been?

716
00:39:01,026 --> 00:39:03,404
‎Oh, good, thanks to you.

717
00:39:04,196 --> 00:39:07,491
‎Listen, I wanted to give you a call

718
00:39:07,575 --> 00:39:09,535
‎because I have news about my grandson.

719
00:39:09,618 --> 00:39:11,454
‎Did something happen to Prosecutor Ma?

720
00:39:11,537 --> 00:39:15,332
‎Ah, it's not bad news at all. Quite
‎the opposite. It's something wonderful.

721
00:39:16,584 --> 00:39:18,919
‎My Gang-uk just told me
‎he met an amazing woman,

722
00:39:19,003 --> 00:39:20,754
‎and he's finally going to get married.

723
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:23,799
‎They're having
‎the engagement ceremony first.

724
00:39:23,883 --> 00:39:24,717
‎That'll happen soon.

725
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:27,094
‎He told me they'll figure out
‎the wedding later.

726
00:39:27,178 --> 00:39:30,097
‎Oh! That's wonderful. Congratulations.

727
00:39:30,723 --> 00:39:32,349
‎I appreciate that.

728
00:39:33,309 --> 00:39:36,312
‎This is all thanks to Ji-hwan and to you.

729
00:39:36,395 --> 00:39:37,855
‎I'm so, um…

730
00:39:39,648 --> 00:39:44,028
‎I'm so thankful, and I'm so sorry.

731
00:39:50,451 --> 00:39:53,746
‎No. Don't be, I'm happy for you.

732
00:39:55,581 --> 00:39:58,125
‎What's she like?
‎Your future granddaughter-in-law.

733
00:39:58,709 --> 00:40:02,087
‎Oh, well, if I'm being honest,

734
00:40:02,171 --> 00:40:04,215
‎she's almost too good for Gang-uk.

735
00:40:04,298 --> 00:40:07,259
‎I'd be lying if I said
‎I wasn't a little worried.

736
00:40:07,343 --> 00:40:11,889
‎But, you know, Gang-uk says he really
‎likes her, so who am I to object?

737
00:40:12,765 --> 00:40:16,143
‎Oh, of course.
‎As long as he's happy, that's what counts.

738
00:40:16,227 --> 00:40:19,563
‎By the way,
‎we'd love to see you at the ceremony.

739
00:40:19,647 --> 00:40:21,023
‎If you're not too busy, of course.

740
00:40:22,024 --> 00:40:26,820
‎Oh… Uh, I can't.
‎I'm in New York right now.

741
00:40:26,904 --> 00:40:28,405
‎I have a few things to take care of.

742
00:40:29,114 --> 00:40:31,700
‎That's all right.
‎I completely understand, yeah.

743
00:40:31,784 --> 00:40:33,702
‎Best of luck with all your work.

744
00:40:34,537 --> 00:40:37,289
‎And never forget, you can call us anytime.

745
00:40:37,915 --> 00:40:40,334
‎Sure, I will. Congratulations again.

746
00:40:40,417 --> 00:40:42,044
‎Yes, thank you.

747
00:40:42,127 --> 00:40:43,254
‎Thank you so much.

748
00:40:43,337 --> 00:40:46,173
‎[somber music playing]

749
00:40:52,763 --> 00:40:54,682
‎[nurse]
‎The donor's heart has been removed, sir.

750
00:40:58,811 --> 00:40:59,645
‎[Gang-uk] Grandma?

751
00:41:05,526 --> 00:41:07,361
‎[no audible dialogue]

752
00:41:07,444 --> 00:41:10,155
‎[somber music continues]

753
00:41:38,475 --> 00:41:40,769
‎We have a date for
‎the engagement ceremony.

754
00:41:42,479 --> 00:41:44,481
‎I wanted to come here
‎and tell you that myself.

755
00:41:45,357 --> 00:41:47,359
‎I think it's better than hearing it
‎from someone else.

756
00:41:51,947 --> 00:41:53,407
‎I appreciate that.

757
00:41:55,618 --> 00:41:56,869
‎But I just can't be happy for you.

758
00:41:58,704 --> 00:42:00,914
‎To be honest, I was confident until now.

759
00:42:03,083 --> 00:42:04,793
‎But for the first time,
‎I'm starting to regret it.

760
00:42:05,628 --> 00:42:07,338
‎I should've come back to Korea sooner.

761
00:42:10,257 --> 00:42:12,134
‎Love is all about timing, isn't it?

762
00:42:13,344 --> 00:42:14,386
‎And it seems like…

763
00:42:17,264 --> 00:42:18,432
‎I missed my first chance.

764
00:42:20,726 --> 00:42:22,061
‎First? What do you mean?

765
00:42:22,770 --> 00:42:25,731
‎I know you could tell.
‎You knew I liked you.

766
00:42:29,276 --> 00:42:30,819
‎This really hurts, I'll admit.

767
00:42:33,405 --> 00:42:34,281
‎But Yeo-ri…

768
00:42:35,658 --> 00:42:37,117
‎I'm not giving up.

769
00:42:38,118 --> 00:42:38,952
‎But…

770
00:42:39,912 --> 00:42:42,039
‎from now on,
‎I'll have to do things differently.

771
00:42:45,334 --> 00:42:46,752
‎I'll be going then.

772
00:42:52,257 --> 00:42:54,218
‎[Ha-ri] Oh. Min-hwan.

773
00:42:56,053 --> 00:42:58,514
‎[scoffs] You were just with Yeo-ri, right?

774
00:42:59,264 --> 00:43:02,434
‎So I'm sure you've heard.
‎They have a date for the ceremony.

775
00:43:03,435 --> 00:43:04,603
‎What?

776
00:43:05,437 --> 00:43:07,981
‎I thought you had a plan or something.
‎You were so confident the other day.

777
00:43:09,233 --> 00:43:10,984
‎Not right now, okay?

778
00:43:22,871 --> 00:43:24,748
‎-Prosecutor Ma!
‎-[Gang-uk] Oh, hey.

779
00:43:25,374 --> 00:43:26,959
‎How are you? Any lunch plans today?

780
00:43:27,042 --> 00:43:28,377
‎Uh, well…

781
00:43:28,460 --> 00:43:31,296
‎Oh, that's great.
‎How about we have lunch together?

782
00:43:31,380 --> 00:43:33,507
‎I, uh… I've got some people
‎I want you to meet.

783
00:43:34,258 --> 00:43:35,759
‎-Oh, okay.
‎-Great.

784
00:43:35,843 --> 00:43:37,511
‎All right!

785
00:43:38,095 --> 00:43:41,932
‎Prosecutor Ma, this isn't a party
‎anyone can crash, you know?

786
00:43:42,015 --> 00:43:43,892
‎We heard you're marrying into Reina,

787
00:43:43,976 --> 00:43:45,936
‎so we thought we'd make
‎an exception for you.

788
00:43:46,019 --> 00:43:46,895
‎[seniors laugh]

789
00:43:46,979 --> 00:43:48,230
‎Well, some people have been calling us

790
00:43:48,313 --> 00:43:50,065
‎"gold-diggers" or "the kept men"
‎or whatever.

791
00:43:50,149 --> 00:43:52,317
‎But you know what?
‎They're just jealous of us.

792
00:43:52,401 --> 00:43:57,489
‎Oh, yeah, for sure. Totally. Oh, by the
‎way, I appreciate the help the other day.

793
00:43:57,573 --> 00:43:59,074
‎Oh, don't mention it. [laughs]

794
00:43:59,158 --> 00:44:00,451
‎Mention what?

795
00:44:00,534 --> 00:44:03,620
‎My brother-in-law got in trouble.
‎A bribery case. He was found guilty.

796
00:44:03,704 --> 00:44:06,498
‎This guy got him to retire
‎without a stain on his record.

797
00:44:06,582 --> 00:44:08,292
‎Thanks to you I saved face with my family.

798
00:44:08,375 --> 00:44:11,295
‎-Glad to hear it. Anytime, huh?
‎-[seniors laugh]

799
00:44:11,378 --> 00:44:15,591
‎Hey, Park. Don't forget about me, man.
‎I got your dumb brother-in-law

800
00:44:15,674 --> 00:44:16,884
‎a cushy job with my wife's company.

801
00:44:16,967 --> 00:44:20,137
‎Yeah, of course. And I'm grateful
‎for that. But hey, come on.

802
00:44:20,220 --> 00:44:21,555
‎I did you a favor too.
‎I didn't leave you hanging.

803
00:44:21,638 --> 00:44:23,891
‎There was that labor law case
‎against your wife.

804
00:44:23,974 --> 00:44:25,392
‎I got her and her company off the hook.

805
00:44:25,476 --> 00:44:26,643
‎[seniors laugh]

806
00:44:26,727 --> 00:44:27,728
‎-Cheers.
‎-Cheers!

807
00:44:27,811 --> 00:44:30,063
‎-Cheers, guys! Let's drink! Okay.
‎-Cheers.

808
00:44:32,983 --> 00:44:35,444
‎All right, so, Prosecutor Ma.

809
00:44:35,527 --> 00:44:37,529
‎There's a price
‎for joining our circle, okay? [chuckles]

810
00:44:38,489 --> 00:44:41,825
‎Nothing crazy.
‎We heard Reina's country clubs are nice.

811
00:44:41,909 --> 00:44:43,911
‎You could get us in there for free, right?

812
00:44:43,994 --> 00:44:46,288
‎[all laugh]

813
00:44:46,955 --> 00:44:50,250
‎-Ah, maybe in your dreams, I could.
‎-What?

814
00:44:50,334 --> 00:44:53,253
‎Come on, if you want to go golfing,
‎maybe try paying for it yourselves.

815
00:44:53,921 --> 00:44:57,591
‎I'm gonna have to let the Inspection
‎Office know about what I heard.

816
00:44:59,051 --> 00:45:01,553
‎Man. I'd pay good money
‎to unhear all that.

817
00:45:03,931 --> 00:45:05,265
‎That pissed me off, geez.

818
00:45:14,775 --> 00:45:17,319
‎[senior] ‎Turns out he's even
‎more insufferable than I expected.

819
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:21,198
‎Anyway, I checked him out,
‎but there wasn't much there.

820
00:45:21,281 --> 00:45:22,991
‎And I don't think
‎we have the time to set him up.

821
00:45:23,075 --> 00:45:24,701
‎The window's pretty narrow.

822
00:45:25,619 --> 00:45:29,665
‎For now, the only thing we can do is
‎transfer him somewhere outside the city.

823
00:45:29,748 --> 00:45:30,999
‎How does that sound?

824
00:45:31,083 --> 00:45:32,751
‎I doubt it'll make much of a difference.

825
00:45:33,502 --> 00:45:36,338
‎But thanks anyway.
‎I owe you one. Let's get together soon.

826
00:45:36,421 --> 00:45:37,464
‎Sounds good, see you soon.

827
00:45:41,635 --> 00:45:43,804
‎CIVIL SERVANT PERSONNEL FILE

828
00:45:52,688 --> 00:45:54,690
‎[line ringing]

829
00:45:55,566 --> 00:45:56,858
‎Vice President, hi.

830
00:45:57,985 --> 00:45:59,194
‎[chuckles] Least I can do.

831
00:45:59,278 --> 00:46:01,196
‎We've been with your bank
‎for years, right?

832
00:46:01,905 --> 00:46:03,657
‎I'd love to stop by, if you don't mind.

833
00:46:05,325 --> 00:46:06,285
‎Yes, great.

834
00:46:07,411 --> 00:46:09,830
‎Actually, I was hoping
‎I could ask you for a favor.

835
00:46:09,913 --> 00:46:11,832
‎-[knocking on door]
‎-Oh, I think he's here.

836
00:46:14,418 --> 00:46:16,753
‎[chuckles] How are you?
‎How are things going?

837
00:46:16,837 --> 00:46:18,714
‎Director Gong,
‎we're so happy you could make it.

838
00:46:19,423 --> 00:46:20,757
‎Uh, wait a minute, who is "we"?

839
00:46:20,841 --> 00:46:24,553
‎Mr. Kang Min-hwan and I.
‎He's the CEO of CL. You know him, right?

840
00:46:25,846 --> 00:46:28,724
‎Oh, wow. It's been quite some time, yes.

841
00:46:28,807 --> 00:46:29,933
‎Uh, what are you doing here?

842
00:46:30,017 --> 00:46:34,563
‎We do most of our banking here as well.
‎I was hoping we'd get a chance to meet.

843
00:46:34,646 --> 00:46:36,106
‎Glad I bumped into you.

844
00:46:38,108 --> 00:46:40,527
‎How did you find out
‎about the loan I took out

845
00:46:40,611 --> 00:46:42,446
‎using Reina's shares as collateral?

846
00:46:44,781 --> 00:46:46,408
‎The loan's almost due.

847
00:46:46,491 --> 00:46:49,453
‎But I don't think you can afford
‎to cover it, can you?

848
00:46:49,536 --> 00:46:53,957
‎[sighs] Well, if this keeps up,
‎they're gonna end up taking the shares.

849
00:46:54,041 --> 00:46:55,459
‎Maybe I could help somehow.

850
00:46:57,544 --> 00:46:58,962
‎I don't get it, why?

851
00:47:00,881 --> 00:47:03,467
‎Is CL interested in Reina, by any chance?

852
00:47:03,550 --> 00:47:06,261
‎No, that's not it. Wait, I know.

853
00:47:06,345 --> 00:47:08,930
‎I have a feeling it's because
‎of Ms. Cheon Yeo-ri, is that right?

854
00:47:09,014 --> 00:47:10,015
‎I get it.

855
00:47:10,098 --> 00:47:12,559
‎She's made some
‎rather unexpected decisions.

856
00:47:12,643 --> 00:47:15,520
‎Everybody in this industry
‎knows about your feelings for her.

857
00:47:15,604 --> 00:47:18,315
‎And if I remember right,
‎you've been friends since you were kids.

858
00:47:18,398 --> 00:47:20,567
‎Given the circumstances,

859
00:47:20,651 --> 00:47:22,778
‎I thought you'd be the obvious choice,

860
00:47:22,861 --> 00:47:24,821
‎even from a strategic standpoint.

861
00:47:25,364 --> 00:47:27,783
‎We can always change
‎the circumstances if we need to.

862
00:47:28,659 --> 00:47:30,118
‎If I were to do something,

863
00:47:30,869 --> 00:47:33,038
‎your shares would be a valuable asset.

864
00:47:42,964 --> 00:47:46,510
‎BAEK GYEONG-JA

865
00:47:48,303 --> 00:47:50,639
‎The FSS was notified of changes
‎in the stock holdings.

866
00:47:51,431 --> 00:47:53,350
‎Who was it? Director Ok? How much?

867
00:47:53,433 --> 00:47:55,811
‎Well, it's, um,
‎somewhat concerning, ma'am.

868
00:47:55,894 --> 00:47:57,854
‎If this escalates any further,

869
00:47:57,938 --> 00:48:01,024
‎Gashin Group's vote
‎could end up being the deciding factor.

870
00:48:01,108 --> 00:48:02,734
‎[sighs]

871
00:48:02,818 --> 00:48:05,237
‎-[groans]
‎-Uh, are you okay, ma'am?

872
00:48:06,738 --> 00:48:08,740
‎Yeo-ri. Call Yeo-ri.

873
00:48:08,824 --> 00:48:10,158
‎Okay. Right away.

874
00:48:17,749 --> 00:48:19,751
‎[panting] Grandma.

875
00:48:22,462 --> 00:48:23,755
‎Wang, what's going on?

876
00:48:23,839 --> 00:48:25,549
‎She suddenly started feeling unwell,

877
00:48:25,632 --> 00:48:27,801
‎so she came in just for a few tests.

878
00:48:27,884 --> 00:48:29,594
‎This is the second time
‎this has happened to you.

879
00:48:29,678 --> 00:48:31,012
‎What can I say?

880
00:48:31,096 --> 00:48:34,141
‎At this age,
‎I can't take my health for granted, can I?

881
00:48:34,224 --> 00:48:35,600
‎[chuckles]

882
00:48:35,684 --> 00:48:37,060
‎Yeo-ri.

883
00:48:37,144 --> 00:48:38,520
‎No time to waste now.

884
00:48:38,603 --> 00:48:39,896
‎We need to expedite it.

885
00:48:39,980 --> 00:48:42,774
‎Not just the wedding,
‎the engagement ceremony.

886
00:48:43,483 --> 00:48:45,652
‎So we can transfer the shares
‎to Prosecutor Ma.

887
00:48:45,736 --> 00:48:46,737
‎Can you do that?

888
00:48:46,820 --> 00:48:48,947
‎It's been done before, right?

889
00:48:49,030 --> 00:48:50,824
‎Yes. The latest case was at PA Group.

890
00:48:50,907 --> 00:48:54,077
‎They gifted around 200,000 shares
‎to their son-in-law

891
00:48:54,161 --> 00:48:55,704
‎when he married into the family.

892
00:48:56,288 --> 00:48:57,789
‎[Baek] It's just a precaution.

893
00:48:58,331 --> 00:49:02,586
‎The FSS received a report
‎of a change to the stock holdings.

894
00:49:02,669 --> 00:49:04,087
‎At this rate,

895
00:49:04,171 --> 00:49:07,174
‎they could call an emergency meeting
‎with the shareholders, right?

896
00:49:08,091 --> 00:49:11,094
‎They're doing the exact same thing
‎they did six years ago.

897
00:49:11,178 --> 00:49:15,474
‎But this time, the agenda
‎will be my removal as CEO.

898
00:49:31,948 --> 00:49:33,617
‎THE ENGAGEMENT OF MS. CHEON YEO-RI,
‎ELDEST DAUGHTER AND HEIRESS OF REINA

899
00:49:33,700 --> 00:49:35,368
‎AND MR. MA GANG-UK, PROSECUTOR, SEOUL
‎CENTRAL DISTRICT PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

900
00:49:35,452 --> 00:49:36,620
‎WILL BE HELD PRIVATELY
‎AT SIENA HALL OF REINA HOTEL

901
00:49:43,418 --> 00:49:45,462
‎12 YEARS AGO

902
00:49:45,545 --> 00:49:47,088
‎-Where are you going?
‎-Oh.

903
00:49:47,798 --> 00:49:49,549
‎I'm going out with Yeo-ri today.
‎I told you.

904
00:49:49,633 --> 00:49:52,469
‎But your father's coming back
‎from his business trip today, Ji-hwan.

905
00:49:52,552 --> 00:49:53,386
‎Can't it wait?

906
00:49:53,470 --> 00:49:56,556
‎Come on, you know Dad goes on those trips
‎every other week.

907
00:49:57,140 --> 00:49:58,642
‎This is the first time
‎I'm going out with Yeo-ri.

908
00:49:58,725 --> 00:50:01,603
‎Yeo-ri this, Yeo-ri that.
‎Goodness, it's always Yeo-ri.

909
00:50:01,686 --> 00:50:03,313
‎Does Yeo-ri know you're like this?

910
00:50:03,396 --> 00:50:06,650
‎Not yet. I'm planning
‎on telling her how I feel today.

911
00:50:06,733 --> 00:50:09,236
‎One girl comes along,
‎and you toss your parents aside?

912
00:50:09,319 --> 00:50:11,196
‎All right.
‎Be careful with that knife, Mom.

913
00:50:11,947 --> 00:50:14,115
‎Hey, wait. Ji-hwan.
‎Ji-hwan, wait a minute.

914
00:50:14,199 --> 00:50:15,200
‎What?

915
00:50:15,992 --> 00:50:17,369
‎Your pendant, where is it?

916
00:50:17,452 --> 00:50:19,913
‎-Oh, the pendant? Huh?
‎-Yeah.

917
00:50:21,122 --> 00:50:21,957
‎[gasps]

918
00:50:23,542 --> 00:50:25,961
‎-What, this one?
‎-[exhales heavily]

919
00:50:26,044 --> 00:50:28,964
‎Why on earth do you have it
‎in your pocket? What if you lose it?

920
00:50:29,047 --> 00:50:30,924
‎You have to keep it around your neck,
‎like I told you.

921
00:50:31,007 --> 00:50:31,842
‎Turn around.

922
00:50:31,925 --> 00:50:34,177
‎It's not my style.
‎It just looks kinda tacky.

923
00:50:35,679 --> 00:50:37,514
‎You can't leave my house

924
00:50:37,597 --> 00:50:39,599
‎if you don't have this pendant
‎around your neck.

925
00:50:39,683 --> 00:50:41,518
‎Understood? Grandma was very specific.

926
00:50:41,601 --> 00:50:42,602
‎Grandma…

927
00:50:42,686 --> 00:50:44,896
‎You have to wear it. She made me promise
‎I wouldn't let you take it off.

928
00:50:44,980 --> 00:50:47,190
‎[sighs] Mom.

929
00:50:49,109 --> 00:50:50,443
‎You know this makes no sense, right?

930
00:50:51,403 --> 00:50:52,779
‎It's just a pendant.

931
00:50:52,863 --> 00:50:54,823
‎How's it supposed to keep ghosts away?

932
00:50:54,906 --> 00:50:56,366
‎I know it sounds drastic.

933
00:50:56,449 --> 00:50:58,285
‎Not everything can be explained
‎by science, son.

934
00:50:59,452 --> 00:51:01,913
‎Just trust her. She cares about you.

935
00:51:01,997 --> 00:51:03,957
‎She'd be worried sick
‎if you stopped wearing it.

936
00:51:04,040 --> 00:51:06,418
‎So just think of it as doing her a favor.

937
00:51:06,501 --> 00:51:09,337
‎Keep it on,
‎and it'll make her feel better. All right?

938
00:51:09,421 --> 00:51:11,548
‎Why's it only me, though?
‎We're twins, aren't we?

939
00:51:11,631 --> 00:51:13,466
‎You don't make Min-hwan wear one.

940
00:51:13,550 --> 00:51:15,302
‎Does she think I'm gonna die young?

941
00:51:15,385 --> 00:51:16,761
‎-[gasps]
‎-Ji-hwan,

942
00:51:16,845 --> 00:51:18,972
‎-how could you say something like that?
‎-Ouch, Mom.

943
00:51:19,055 --> 00:51:21,141
‎I'm just saying,
‎she worries too much about me.

944
00:51:21,224 --> 00:51:24,227
‎-Ji-hwan.
‎-Hey, bro. Are you ready?

945
00:51:24,978 --> 00:51:28,315
‎Don't worry, I'll take good care of him.
‎We won't be out too long.

946
00:51:28,398 --> 00:51:30,108
‎Okay, hope you have a good time.

947
00:51:30,191 --> 00:51:32,402
‎-Take care.
‎-All right.

948
00:51:32,485 --> 00:51:33,737
‎Try not to worry too much, okay?

949
00:51:39,784 --> 00:51:41,036
‎See you soon, Mom.

950
00:51:45,457 --> 00:51:49,127
‎You really think something like this
‎can keep ghosts away?

951
00:51:49,210 --> 00:51:51,755
‎[groaning]

952
00:51:51,838 --> 00:51:54,174
‎[Ji-hwan] You live. I'll die instead.

953
00:51:54,257 --> 00:51:55,592
‎-[wave surges]
‎-[ghostly hissing]

954
00:51:56,801 --> 00:51:58,178
‎[screams]

955
00:52:04,768 --> 00:52:05,894
‎[Ji-hwan] Yeo-ri!

956
00:52:05,977 --> 00:52:08,939
‎[panting]

957
00:52:29,334 --> 00:52:30,168
‎[Ji-hwan] ‎Min-hwan.

958
00:52:32,253 --> 00:52:33,296
‎Min-hwan!

959
00:52:34,339 --> 00:52:35,340
‎Listen to me!

960
00:52:45,934 --> 00:52:49,771
‎KANG MIN-HWAN

961
00:53:06,246 --> 00:53:07,789
‎[Ji-uk]
‎What's the key to a good croissant?

962
00:53:07,872 --> 00:53:08,790
‎[employee] The crispiness.

963
00:53:08,873 --> 00:53:10,959
‎Exactly. If it's not crispy,
‎you replace it right away.

964
00:53:11,042 --> 00:53:11,918
‎-Got it?
‎-Will do.

965
00:53:12,002 --> 00:53:13,795
‎[Ji-uk] We can't have people
‎eating soggy croissants.

966
00:53:13,878 --> 00:53:14,754
‎[employee] Got it.

967
00:53:14,838 --> 00:53:17,507
‎And keep an eye on the wine.
‎Keep it topped off at all times, okay?

968
00:53:17,590 --> 00:53:19,134
‎-[employee] Will do, sir.
‎-Check if any guests have allergies.

969
00:53:19,217 --> 00:53:20,385
‎She runs a strawberry farm.

970
00:53:20,468 --> 00:53:23,513
‎-That was really nice of her, right?
‎-Hope you enjoy it.

971
00:53:23,596 --> 00:53:24,931
‎[line ringing]

972
00:53:26,307 --> 00:53:29,269
‎[automated voice] ‎The person you are
‎trying to reach is currently unavailable.

973
00:53:34,274 --> 00:53:35,692
‎[line ringing]

974
00:53:38,361 --> 00:53:39,362
‎CHEON YEO-RI AND MA GANG-UK

975
00:53:39,446 --> 00:53:40,780
‎WITH THE TRUST AND LOVE
‎WE HAVE FOR EACH OTHER,

976
00:53:40,864 --> 00:53:42,449
‎WE ARE HERE TO PROMISE
‎TO BECOME LIFELONG PARTNERS

977
00:53:42,532 --> 00:53:44,909
‎[rain pattering]

978
00:53:44,993 --> 00:53:47,037
‎[thunder rumbling]

979
00:53:54,836 --> 00:53:56,838
‎[ominous music playing]

980
00:54:02,594 --> 00:54:03,803
‎[phone buzzing]

981
00:54:03,887 --> 00:54:05,472
‎INCOMING CALL
‎GANG-UK

982
00:54:07,307 --> 00:54:09,350
‎-Gang-uk?
‎-[Gang-uk] ‎Hey, sorry.

983
00:54:09,434 --> 00:54:11,770
‎I kept getting calls from work,
‎so I couldn't answer when you called.

984
00:54:13,980 --> 00:54:15,023
‎No problem, where are you?

985
00:54:15,106 --> 00:54:18,109
‎I'm in the parking lot,
‎almost at the elevator.

986
00:54:18,818 --> 00:54:20,570
‎So you've made it to the hotel already.

987
00:54:20,653 --> 00:54:22,906
‎Yeah. I'm in the elevator now.

988
00:54:24,240 --> 00:54:25,241
‎I'll be right up.

989
00:54:25,909 --> 00:54:27,786
‎-Yeo-ri, listen…
‎-[line disconnects]

990
00:54:27,869 --> 00:54:29,037
‎Hmm?

991
00:54:29,120 --> 00:54:31,372
‎CALL ENDED

992
00:54:36,211 --> 00:54:37,962
‎-[clanging]
‎-[gasps]

993
00:54:39,380 --> 00:54:41,424
‎Whoa. What was that?

994
00:54:41,508 --> 00:54:43,760
‎[tense music playing]

995
00:54:43,843 --> 00:54:47,263
‎[automated voice] ‎The person you are
‎trying to reach is currently unavailable.

996
00:54:56,898 --> 00:54:59,192
‎-Min-hwan.
‎-I have something to say to you.

997
00:54:59,859 --> 00:55:00,902
‎Uh, right now?

998
00:55:01,778 --> 00:55:04,114
‎Sorry, it'll have to wait.
‎I… I have to step out now.

999
00:55:04,197 --> 00:55:05,824
‎I've already waited too long.

1000
00:55:07,951 --> 00:55:09,244
‎I came to Korea

1001
00:55:10,161 --> 00:55:11,830
‎when I heard about
‎your engagement six years ago.

1002
00:55:14,749 --> 00:55:16,876
‎I was set on changing
‎your mind, no matter what.

1003
00:55:16,960 --> 00:55:18,586
‎[Gi-u] Don't come any closer!

1004
00:55:18,670 --> 00:55:19,963
‎-[panting]
‎-[Yeo-ri] Gi-u, wait.

1005
00:55:20,046 --> 00:55:21,381
‎[Gi-u] I said don't come closer!

1006
00:55:22,507 --> 00:55:27,053
‎I didn't think just holding your hand
‎would have them haunt me like that.

1007
00:55:29,347 --> 00:55:30,765
‎I'm sorry.

1008
00:55:30,849 --> 00:55:33,351
‎I don't think I can do this. I'm sorry.

1009
00:55:43,027 --> 00:55:47,657
‎But I couldn't just walk up to you
‎when you were hurting so much.

1010
00:55:49,993 --> 00:55:51,744
‎I'll admit it, I felt relieved too.

1011
00:55:54,205 --> 00:55:56,416
‎That got me thinking
‎I still had a chance with you.

1012
00:55:59,252 --> 00:56:00,628
‎Now I wonder if I'm too late.

1013
00:56:02,380 --> 00:56:03,673
‎And here we are again.

1014
00:56:05,633 --> 00:56:10,180
‎Yeo-ri… I've had feelings for you
‎for a very long time.

1015
00:56:12,515 --> 00:56:14,225
‎I don't wanna watch you slip away again.

1016
00:56:17,896 --> 00:56:20,815
‎Min-hwan, I'm sorry.

1017
00:56:21,774 --> 00:56:23,776
‎I've never thought of you that way.

1018
00:56:25,028 --> 00:56:25,862
‎Yeo-ri.

1019
00:56:25,945 --> 00:56:27,614
‎Just talking about this
‎with you feels weird.

1020
00:56:27,697 --> 00:56:29,490
‎I'm sorry, but I can't.

1021
00:56:33,369 --> 00:56:34,537
‎What if he doesn't show up?

1022
00:56:35,580 --> 00:56:37,081
‎Like what happened to you last time?

1023
00:56:43,296 --> 00:56:44,756
‎Are you sure you wanna be alone again?

1024
00:56:50,637 --> 00:56:52,513
‎-Huh?
‎-[ghostly hissing]

1025
00:56:54,098 --> 00:56:57,143
‎[melancholy music playing]

1026
00:56:57,227 --> 00:56:59,854
‎Yeo-ri. You can hold my hand.

1027
00:57:05,235 --> 00:57:06,152
‎Damn it.

1028
00:57:28,007 --> 00:57:29,676
‎[Gang-uk] Excuse me! Hello!

1029
00:57:29,759 --> 00:57:31,761
‎Hello! I'm stuck in here! I'm stuck!

1030
00:57:37,809 --> 00:57:39,811
‎[melancholy music continues]

1031
00:57:53,283 --> 00:57:54,826
‎[Min-hwan, echoing]
‎What if he doesn't show up?

1032
00:57:54,909 --> 00:57:56,536
‎Like what happened to you the last time?

1033
00:57:58,371 --> 00:57:59,664
‎[elevator button rattling]

1034
00:57:59,747 --> 00:58:02,041
‎[Gang-uk]
‎Hello! The doors won't open! I'm stuck!

1035
00:58:02,125 --> 00:58:05,044
‎[ghostly whispering]

1036
00:58:05,128 --> 00:58:06,713
‎[Gi-u] ‎I said don't come closer!

1037
00:58:06,796 --> 00:58:09,215
‎I didn't think just holding your hand

1038
00:58:09,299 --> 00:58:10,967
‎would have them
‎haunt me like that. ‎[echoing]

1039
00:58:11,050 --> 00:58:12,760
‎[Min-hwan, echoing]
‎Like what happened to you the least time.

1040
00:58:12,844 --> 00:58:14,846
‎-[Gang-uk] Hello!
‎-[ghostly whispering]

1041
00:58:17,015 --> 00:58:19,976
‎[Gi-u] ‎I'm sorry.
‎I don't think I can do this. I'm sorry.

1042
00:58:20,059 --> 00:58:21,311
‎I won't see her again.

1043
00:58:21,394 --> 00:58:22,979
‎-I won't see Yeo-ri ever again.
‎-[Gang-uk] Leave me alone!

1044
00:58:23,062 --> 00:58:24,522
‎[whispering intensifies]

1045
00:58:24,606 --> 00:58:26,065
‎Leave me alone!

1046
00:58:26,149 --> 00:58:28,192
‎[panting]

1047
00:58:45,084 --> 00:58:48,171
‎[romantic music playing]

1048
00:59:06,606 --> 00:59:08,650
‎[Gang-uk] Y-Yeo-ri, are you okay?

1049
00:59:14,656 --> 00:59:15,740
‎Gang-uk.

1050
00:59:17,283 --> 00:59:19,327
‎I'm sorry, the elevator
‎stopped out of nowhere.

1051
00:59:19,410 --> 00:59:20,453
‎But I'm here now.

1052
00:59:23,748 --> 00:59:25,750
‎I didn't think you were going to show.

1053
00:59:25,833 --> 00:59:27,877
‎Why wouldn't I be here?

1054
00:59:27,960 --> 00:59:29,629
‎I've been waiting for this day.

1055
00:59:36,719 --> 00:59:37,929
‎Before we go inside…

1056
00:59:38,680 --> 00:59:42,100
‎Here. I wasn't sure what you'd like,
‎so I picked something myself.

1057
00:59:44,143 --> 00:59:45,561
‎Um, what do you think?

1058
01:00:14,716 --> 01:00:16,467
‎For a moment, I was so scared.

1059
01:00:19,887 --> 01:00:21,472
‎I thought the ghosts scared you away.

1060
01:00:23,891 --> 01:00:27,270
‎I thought it was all falling apart,
‎like it did last time.

1061
01:00:27,353 --> 01:00:28,688
‎But then I realized…

1062
01:00:30,773 --> 01:00:32,525
‎that's not what really scared me.

1063
01:00:37,196 --> 01:00:39,449
‎I was just scared
‎you wouldn't be here with me.

1064
01:00:41,993 --> 01:00:42,994
‎That I wouldn't…

1065
01:00:44,912 --> 01:00:46,539
‎be able to see you anymore.

1066
01:00:49,250 --> 01:00:51,294
‎I couldn't bear the thought of that.

1067
01:00:54,255 --> 01:00:55,548
‎Well, I promised you.

1068
01:00:56,382 --> 01:00:57,592
‎Don't ever be scared.

1069
01:00:58,301 --> 01:01:00,553
‎Wherever you are,
‎I'll always be there for you.

1070
01:01:08,227 --> 01:01:09,228
‎Gang-uk,

1071
01:01:10,480 --> 01:01:12,607
‎I want to be engaged to you.

1072
01:01:14,525 --> 01:01:16,444
‎And I actually want to marry you.

1073
01:01:30,124 --> 01:01:31,125
‎Gang-uk,

1074
01:01:32,502 --> 01:01:34,086
‎will you be my fiancé?

1075
01:01:47,266 --> 01:01:49,352
‎[upbeat music playing]

1076
01:02:58,880 --> 01:03:01,799
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

1077
01:03:02,592 --> 01:03:05,303
‎[Ha-ri] ‎Cheon Yeo-ri's engagement
‎ceremony has a huge impact on Siena.

1078
01:03:05,386 --> 01:03:08,097
‎[Yeo-ri] ‎Reina will hold
‎an extraordinary general meeting soon.

1079
01:03:09,015 --> 01:03:10,016
‎[Gang-uk] ‎Is it a serious situation?

1080
01:03:10,099 --> 01:03:13,227
‎The dismissal of Cheon Yeo-ri,
‎CEO of Reina Hotels.

1081
01:03:13,311 --> 01:03:16,355
‎-How bold of Ok Gye-hui.
‎-[Ha-ri] ‎Then when will they start?

1082
01:03:16,439 --> 01:03:17,398
‎Right away.

1083
01:03:17,481 --> 01:03:19,233
‎Please give us your support!

1084
01:03:19,317 --> 01:03:20,151
‎[all] Cheers!

1085
01:03:20,234 --> 01:03:21,903
‎Who are the shareholders
‎worth approaching?

1086
01:03:21,986 --> 01:03:24,071
‎-You'll do it yourself, Ms. Cheon?
‎-I have to.

1087
01:03:24,155 --> 01:03:25,865
‎[Gang-uk] ‎Whatever it is you need,
‎tell me. I'll help you with everything.

1088
01:03:25,948 --> 01:03:27,575
‎-I won't do it, I won't do it.
‎-No, no, wait, wait.

1089
01:03:28,576 --> 01:03:30,036
‎[Baek]
‎I'm going on a business trip abroad.

1090
01:03:30,119 --> 01:03:31,579
‎[Ha-ri]
‎Cheon Yeo-ri must be really desperate

1091
01:03:31,662 --> 01:03:32,955
‎to resort to something this ridiculous.

1092
01:03:33,039 --> 01:03:36,459
‎[Min-hwan] ‎It may be impetuous,
‎but I've got to try another approach.

1093
01:03:36,542 --> 01:03:37,668
‎Is Kang Min-hwan going too?

1094
01:03:39,462 --> 01:03:41,339
‎I think I should also go with you.

